window.CLF_EXAMS=window.CLF_EXAMS||[];
window.CLF_EXAMS.push({"id":3,"qs":[{"id":"E1B-60","d":1,"ts":"1.2.8","t":"Asynchronous data API pattern","q":"A company exposes an API that lets internal applications request custom reports. Each request runs an Amazon Athena query that takes 2 to 5 minutes. Clients currently call an Amazon API Gateway REST API that synchronously invokes an AWS Lambda function, and most requests time out before the query completes. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Increase the Lambda function timeout to 15 minutes.","Increase the memory of the Lambda function so that the query completes faster.","Enable API Gateway caching so that subsequent requests return quickly.","Change the API to an asynchronous pattern: one endpoint starts the Athena query and returns the query execution ID, and another endpoint returns the status and the results location when the query is complete."],"a":[3],"e":"Penentunya adalah query yang memakan '2 to 5 minutes' dan panggilan sinkron melalui API Gateway yang membuat 'most requests time out'. Integrasi API Gateway REST memiliki batas waktu integrasi default 29 detik; untuk Regional dan private REST API batas ini bisa dinaikkan melalui permintaan kenaikan kuota (yang mungkin mengurangi kuota throttle akun), tetapi menahan request HTTP sinkron selama beberapa menit tetap bukan desain yang baik untuk pekerjaan panjang. Pola asinkron, yaitu endpoint yang memulai query dan mengembalikan ID eksekusi lalu endpoint lain untuk mengecek status dan lokasi hasil di S3, menghindari timeout sama sekali. Menaikkan timeout Lambda adalah distraktor yang menggoda, tetapi API Gateway tetap memutus koneksi sebelum Lambda selesai. Memori Lambda tidak mempercepat Athena. Caching tidak membantu karena setiap laporan bersifat kustom dan request pertama tetap timeout. Aturan umum: pekerjaan data yang panjang di balik API → pola asinkron (submit lalu poll, atau notifikasi).","r":["Salah — Timeout Lambda bukan penyebabnya; API Gateway memutus request sinkron setelah batas integrasi (default 29 detik) walaupun Lambda masih berjalan.","Salah — Memori Lambda tidak memengaruhi durasi query Athena.","Salah — Laporan kustom jarang identik, dan request pertama tetap timeout.","Benar — Pola submit-and-poll menghindari batas waktu integrasi API Gateway untuk query berdurasi menit."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'long-running query behind API Gateway times out' → asynchronous pattern (start query, return ID, poll for results)."},{"id":"E3B-40","d":3,"ts":"3.4.1","t":"Glue Data Quality row-level outcomes and quarantine","q":"A Glue ETL job validates IoT readings with AWS Glue Data Quality rules. Only a small fraction of rows violate the rules. The business wants valid rows to continue to the curated zone without delay, and invalid rows to be stored separately in a quarantine prefix with the reason they failed for later remediation. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST custom code?","o":["Configure the job to fail when any rule fails and reprocess the whole file manually.","Run a DataBrew profile job on each file and delete the files that contain invalid rows.","Enable row-level outcomes in the Evaluate Data Quality transform and route rows by the DataQualityEvaluationResult column, writing failed rows and their DataQualityRulesFail details to the quarantine prefix.","Write a Lambda function triggered by each S3 upload that validates every row with custom Python code."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya: 'valid rows continue without delay', 'invalid rows stored separately with the reason', dan 'LEAST custom code'. Evaluate Data Quality di Glue dapat menghasilkan row-level outcomes: setiap baris diberi kolom seperti DataQualityEvaluationResult (Passed/Failed) dan DataQualityRulesFail (aturan yang dilanggar). Dengan transform filter/conditional router, baris lolos diteruskan ke curated zone sementara baris gagal ditulis ke prefix karantina beserta alasannya. Distraktor terdekat adalah fail-the-job: menghentikan semua data, termasuk baris valid. Lambda kustom butuh kode validasi sendiri. DataBrew menghapus file utuh dan kehilangan data valid. Aturan: pisahkan baris baik/buruk → row-level outcomes + quarantine.","r":["Salah — Menggagalkan job menahan semua baris valid dan menambah kerja manual.","Salah — Menghapus file utuh menghilangkan baris yang valid dan tidak menyimpan alasan kegagalan.","Benar — Row-level outcomes menandai setiap baris dan aturannya yang gagal sehingga dapat dirutekan ke karantina tanpa kode validasi kustom.","Salah — Validasi kustom di Lambda menambah kode dan tidak memanfaatkan aturan DQ yang sudah ada."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'quarantine bad records, keep good ones flowing' → Glue DQ row-level outcomes."},{"id":"E4A-28","d":4,"ts":"4.1.7","t":"SageMaker Unified Studio group-based project membership","q":"A company's Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio domain is already configured so that employees sign in with single sign-on through the corporate identity provider, and the corporate directory groups are available in the domain. The 'risk-analytics' group has about 60 analysts, and people join and leave the group every month. The owner of the 'credit-risk' project must give every current and future member of this group contributor access to the project with the LEAST ongoing administrative effort. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Add each of the 60 analysts to the 'credit-risk' project individually with the Contributor role, and add or remove analysts as the group changes.","Create an IAM user for each analyst, and add the IAM users to the 'credit-risk' project.","Add the 'risk-analytics' group to the 'credit-risk' project as a single member with the Contributor role, and let the corporate identity provider manage who belongs to the group.","Make the 'risk-analytics' group an owner of the domain unit that contains the 'credit-risk' project."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'every current and future member of this group', 'contributor access to the project', dan 'LEAST ongoing administrative effort'. Di SageMaker Unified Studio, project member bisa berupa user atau group, dan satu group dihitung sebagai satu project member; role yang tersedia adalah Contributor dan Owner. Dengan menambahkan group 'risk-analytics' sebagai Contributor, keanggotaan project mengikuti keanggotaan group di identity provider, sehingga analis baru otomatis mendapat akses dan yang keluar otomatis kehilangan akses. Menambahkan 60 analis satu per satu tidak hanya merepotkan, tetapi juga melampaui batas maksimum 20 member per project. IAM user per analis menambah credential jangka panjang, melewati SSO, dan tetap dikelola per orang. Menjadikan group sebagai owner domain unit memberi wewenang administratif (authorization policy, pengelolaan project) yang jauh melebihi akses contributor ke satu project. Aturan umum: akses project berbasis tim di SageMaker Unified Studio → tambahkan group sebagai project member dengan role seminimal mungkin.","r":["Salah — Mengelola anggota satu per satu menambah pekerjaan rutin, dan 60 member melampaui batas 20 member per project.","Salah — IAM user per analis menambah credential jangka panjang, melewati SSO, dan tetap harus dikelola per orang.","Benar — Group dihitung sebagai satu project member, dan perubahan keanggotaan di identity provider otomatis tercermin pada akses project.","Salah — Kepemilikan domain unit adalah wewenang administratif yang melanggar least privilege dan tidak sama dengan peran contributor di project."],"k":"Tips ujian: akses project SageMaker Unified Studio untuk satu tim → tambahkan group (bukan user satu per satu) sebagai project member; batas 20 member per project, group = 1 member."},{"id":"E3A-27","d":3,"ts":"3.1.7","t":"Athena workgroups","q":"Several teams share one AWS account and run ad hoc Amazon Athena queries. Last month, a single poorly written query scanned 40 TB of data. The data engineering lead wants to stop any single query in the marketing team from scanning more than 1 TB and wants to track Athena usage separately for each team. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create an AWS Budgets alert for Athena and notify the marketing team when the budget is exceeded.","Use an IAM policy condition that limits the number of bytes scanned by athena:StartQueryExecution.","Ask users to add a LIMIT clause to every query.","Create a separate Athena workgroup for each team, set a per-query data usage control of 1 TB on the marketing workgroup, and use the workgroup metrics and tags to track usage."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'stop any single query from scanning more than 1 TB' dan 'track usage separately for each team'. Athena workgroups memisahkan pengguna dan beban kerja; setiap workgroup bisa memiliki per-query data usage control yang membatalkan query saat melewati batas data yang dipindai. Workgroup juga menyediakan metrik CloudWatch dan bisa diberi tag untuk alokasi biaya per tim. AWS Budgets hanya memberi peringatan setelah biaya terjadi, tidak menghentikan query. Tidak ada condition key IAM untuk membatasi jumlah byte yang dipindai. LIMIT hanya membatasi baris output; Athena tetap bisa memindai seluruh data. Aturan umum: kontrol biaya dan isolasi beban kerja Athena per tim → workgroups dengan data usage controls.","r":["Salah — Budgets hanya memberi notifikasi setelah biaya muncul, tidak membatalkan query.","Salah — Tidak ada condition key IAM yang membatasi byte yang dipindai Athena.","Salah — LIMIT membatasi baris hasil, bukan jumlah data yang dipindai.","Benar — Workgroup per tim dengan per-query data usage control membatalkan query di atas 1 TB dan memisahkan pelacakan biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: batasi data scanned per query / pisahkan biaya per tim di Athena → workgroups + data usage controls."},{"id":"E4A-17","d":4,"ts":"4.1.5","t":"S3 Access Points for shared datasets","q":"A shared Amazon S3 data lake bucket is used by 30 teams. Each team needs different permissions to different prefixes, and some teams access the bucket only from specific VPCs. The bucket policy has become very large, is hard to audit, and is close to the bucket policy size limit. Which solution will simplify access management at scale?","o":["Split the bucket policy into multiple bucket policies, one per team.","Replace the bucket policy with S3 object ACLs that grant each team access to its objects.","Use IAM group policies for each team and remove all resource-based policies.","Create an S3 Access Point for each team with its own access point policy (and a VPC network origin where required), and delegate access control from the bucket policy to the access points."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'very large', 'close to the bucket policy size limit', 'specific VPCs'. S3 Access Points memberi setiap aplikasi atau tim hostname dan policy sendiri, sehingga aturan yang tadinya menumpuk di satu bucket policy dipecah menjadi policy per access point yang lebih kecil dan mudah diaudit. Access point bisa dibuat dengan network origin VPC, sehingga hanya bisa diakses dari VPC tertentu. Bucket policy cukup mendelegasikan kontrol ke access point milik akun (misalnya dengan kondisi s3:DataAccessPointAccount). Satu bucket hanya boleh punya satu bucket policy. ACL adalah mekanisme lama yang direkomendasikan untuk dinonaktifkan (Object Ownership: bucket owner enforced). IAM policy saja tidak bisa membatasi asal VPC dengan rapi untuk akses lintas akun. Aturan umum: banyak tim/aplikasi pada satu shared bucket → S3 Access Points.","r":["Salah — Satu bucket hanya dapat memiliki satu bucket policy.","Salah — ACL sulit dikelola, tidak mendukung kondisi seperti VPC, dan AWS menyarankan menonaktifkannya.","Salah — Tanpa resource policy, pembatasan per VPC dan akses lintas akun menjadi sulit; masalah skalabilitas hanya dipindah.","Benar — Access point per tim dengan policy sendiri dan network origin VPC menyederhanakan dan menskalakan pengelolaan akses."],"k":"Tips ujian: shared bucket dengan banyak tim/policy yang membengkak → S3 Access Points (policy per access point, VPC-only access point)."},{"id":"E3B-26","d":3,"ts":"3.3.8","t":"CloudWatch Logs Insights","q":"After a deployment, an AWS Lambda function that transforms incoming records starts failing intermittently. A data engineer needs to find, within the next few minutes, the 10 most frequent error messages in the function's log group over the last 24 hours. Which solution is the MOST efficient?","o":["Export the log group to Amazon S3 and query it with Amazon Athena.","Run a CloudWatch Logs Insights query that filters messages containing ERROR, groups them with stats count(*) by message, and sorts the results in descending order with a limit of 10.","Create a metric filter for ERROR and wait for the metric to accumulate data.","Stream the log group to Amazon OpenSearch Service and build a visualization."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'within the next few minutes' dan analisis ad hoc pada log yang sudah ada di CloudWatch Logs selama '24 hours'. CloudWatch Logs Insights dapat langsung menjalankan query seperti filter @message like /ERROR/ | stats count(*) as c by @message | sort c desc | limit 10 tanpa setup apa pun. Distraktor terdekat adalah ekspor ke S3 + Athena: bisa, tetapi butuh waktu ekspor, definisi tabel, dan langkah tambahan. Metric filter hanya menghitung event BARU setelah dibuat, tidak menganalisis 24 jam terakhir. OpenSearch butuh domain dan streaming. Aturan: analisis ad hoc cepat pada log di CloudWatch → Logs Insights.","r":["Salah — Ekspor dan pembuatan tabel Athena memakan waktu dan langkah tambahan.","Benar — Logs Insights langsung menganalisis log yang ada dan mengelompokkan error berdasarkan frekuensi.","Salah — Metric filter tidak berlaku surut dan hanya memberi hitungan, bukan teks error teratas.","Salah — Butuh domain OpenSearch dan pipeline streaming, terlalu banyak untuk analisis cepat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'quickly query logs already in CloudWatch' → CloudWatch Logs Insights."},{"id":"E2A-15","d":2,"ts":"2.1.2","t":"DynamoDB partition key design","q":"An IoT platform writes sensor readings to an Amazon DynamoDB table that uses the reading date (for example, 2026-10-14) as the partition key and a UUID as the sort key. About 30,000 writes per second arrive and the table frequently returns ProvisionedThroughputExceededException errors, even though total table capacity is well above the write rate. What should a data engineer do to resolve the throttling?","o":["Increase the table's provisioned write capacity units to 3 times the current value.","Switch the table to on-demand capacity mode and keep the same key design.","Add a global secondary index with the reading date as its partition key.","Redesign the table to use device_id as the partition key and the reading timestamp as the sort key."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci adalah throttling terjadi 'even though total table capacity is well above the write rate', dengan partition key berupa tanggal. Semua tulisan pada hari yang sama masuk ke satu partition key sehingga terjadi hot partition; setiap partisi fisik memiliki batas throughput (sekitar 1.000 WCU per partisi), sehingga menambah kapasitas tabel tidak membantu. Solusinya adalah memakai partition key berkardinalitas tinggi yang tersebar merata seperti device_id, dengan timestamp sebagai sort key untuk query rentang waktu per perangkat. Distraktor terdekat adalah on-demand mode: menghilangkan capacity planning, tetapi batas per partisi tetap berlaku sehingga satu key 'panas' tetap di-throttle. GSI dengan date sebagai partition key juga akan panas dan bahkan bisa menahan tulisan tabel dasar. Aturan umum: throttling dengan kapasitas total cukup → masalah desain partition key; gunakan key berkardinalitas tinggi atau write sharding.","r":["Salah — Kapasitas tabel tidak mengatasi batas throughput per partisi; key tanggal tetap mengonsentrasikan tulisan di satu partisi.","Salah — On-demand tidak menghapus batas throughput per partisi, sehingga hot key tetap di-throttle.","Salah — GSI dengan key tanggal akan mengalami hot partition yang sama dan dapat memicu back-pressure ke tabel dasar.","Benar — device_id berkardinalitas tinggi menyebarkan tulisan ke banyak partisi, dan timestamp sebagai sort key tetap mendukung query waktu."],"k":"Throttling padahal kapasitas total cukup → hot partition; ganti ke partition key berkardinalitas tinggi / write sharding."},{"id":"E3A-38","d":3,"ts":"3.2.1","t":"Quick Sight row-level security","q":"A company publishes one Amazon Quick Sight sales dashboard to 60 regional managers. Each manager must see only the rows for their own region, while executives must see all regions. The company does not want to maintain a separate dashboard or dataset for each region. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create 60 copies of the dataset, each filtered to one region, and share each copy with one manager.","Add a region filter control to the dashboard and ask managers to select their own region.","Apply row-level security (RLS) to the dataset by using a rules dataset that maps each user or group to the allowed region values, with executives granted access to all regions.","Create separate IAM roles for each region and restrict access to the S3 objects that hold the source data."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'see only rows for their own region', 'executives see all', dan 'not maintain a separate dashboard or dataset per region'. Row-level security (RLS) di Quick Sight memakai dataset aturan yang memetakan user atau group ke nilai kolom yang boleh dilihat (misalnya region). Satu dataset dan satu dashboard dapat dibagikan ke semua orang, dan setiap pengguna otomatis hanya melihat baris yang diizinkan; baris aturan dengan nilai kosong memberikan akses ke semua nilai untuk eksekutif. Menyalin dataset 60 kali melanggar syarat. Filter control hanya kenyamanan tampilan; pengguna bisa memilih region lain, jadi bukan kontrol keamanan. Pembatasan IAM pada S3 tidak berlaku untuk data yang sudah ada di SPICE dan tidak memfilter baris di dashboard. Aturan umum: 'users see only their rows' di Quick Sight → row-level security.","r":["Salah — 60 salinan dataset menambah beban pemeliharaan, persis yang ingin dihindari.","Salah — Filter control bukan kontrol keamanan; pengguna tetap bisa memilih region lain.","Benar — RLS dengan rules dataset memfilter baris per user/group dari satu dataset dan satu dashboard.","Salah — Izin S3 tidak memfilter baris di dataset SPICE atau dashboard."],"k":"Tips ujian: Quick Sight 'each user sees only their own data' → row-level security (rules dataset)."},{"id":"E2B-50","d":2,"ts":"2.3.5","t":"GDPR deletion with Apache Iceberg","q":"A company stores customer events in an S3 data lake as Apache Iceberg tables that are queried with Amazon Athena. Under GDPR, the company must erase all records of a customer within 30 days of a request, and the deleted data must not remain in older table snapshots or data files. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Run an Athena DELETE statement for the customer's records, run OPTIMIZE REWRITE DATA USING BIN_PACK to rewrite the affected data files, and then run the Athena VACUUM statement to expire old snapshots and remove files that are no longer needed.","Create a Lake Formation row-level filter that hides the customer's records from all users.","Add an S3 Lifecycle rule that expires the table's data files after 30 days.","Rewrite the entire table every week with an AWS Glue job that excludes erased customers."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'erase all records of a customer' dan 'must not remain in older table snapshots or data files'. Athena mendukung DELETE tingkat baris pada tabel Iceberg, tetapi penghapusan ini ditulis sebagai delete file (merge-on-read), sehingga data file asli yang berisi baris tersebut masih ada; snapshot lama untuk time travel juga masih mereferensikannya. OPTIMIZE ... REWRITE DATA USING BIN_PACK menggabungkan delete file ke data file baru tanpa baris tersebut, lalu VACUUM menjalankan expire snapshots dan remove orphan files sesuai properti retensi tabel (default vacuum_max_snapshot_age_seconds 5 hari; role butuh s3:DeleteObject), sehingga data benar-benar hilang dari S3. Row-level filter hanya menyembunyikan data; datanya tetap ada sehingga tidak memenuhi hak penghapusan. Lifecycle expiration berbasis umur file akan menghapus data semua pelanggan. Menulis ulang seluruh tabel setiap minggu mahal dan berat. Ingat: GDPR delete di data lake → table format transaksional (Iceberg) DELETE + OPTIMIZE (rewrite data) + VACUUM.","r":["Benar — DELETE mencatat penghapusan di delete file, OPTIMIZE menulis ulang data file tanpa baris tersebut, dan VACUUM membuang snapshot lama serta file yang tidak lagi dibutuhkan.","Salah — Row filter hanya menyembunyikan data; data tetap tersimpan sehingga tidak memenuhi penghapusan.","Salah — Expiration berbasis umur menghapus semua data, bukan hanya milik pelanggan tertentu.","Salah — Menulis ulang seluruh tabel mingguan mahal dan menambah overhead operasional."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'right to be forgotten' di data lake Iceberg/Athena → DELETE + OPTIMIZE REWRITE DATA + VACUUM (expire snapshots)."},{"id":"E3B-03","d":3,"ts":"3.3.5","t":"CloudTrail Insights","q":"A data platform account runs hundreds of automated pipelines. The security team wants to be informed when the rate of write management API calls (for example, glue:DeleteTable or s3:PutBucketPolicy) deviates significantly from the account's normal baseline, without having to define or tune static thresholds. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Create CloudWatch Logs metric filters for each API name and set static alarm thresholds based on last month's averages.","Enable AWS Config managed rules for Glue and S3 resources.","Enable CloudTrail Insights on the existing trail for API call rate and send Insights events to Amazon EventBridge for notification.","Enable S3 server access logging on all buckets and analyze the logs weekly with Amazon Athena."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah 'deviates significantly from the account's normal baseline' dan 'without having to define or tune static thresholds'. CloudTrail Insights menganalisis management events tipe write, membangun baseline volume panggilan API (API call rate) dan error rate, lalu menghasilkan Insights event saat terjadi lonjakan tidak biasa. Insights events bisa diteruskan ke EventBridge lalu ke SNS. Distraktor terdekat adalah metric filter dengan threshold statis, tetapi itu justru melanggar syarat 'tanpa threshold statis' dan perlu tuning manual. AWS Config fokus pada kepatuhan konfigurasi, bukan anomali volume API. Ingat: 'unusual API activity / baseline' → CloudTrail Insights.","r":["Salah — Threshold statis harus ditentukan dan disetel manual, bertentangan dengan persyaratan.","Salah — AWS Config rules mengevaluasi kepatuhan konfigurasi resource, bukan anomali laju panggilan API.","Benar — CloudTrail Insights otomatis mendeteksi laju write API yang menyimpang dari baseline dan event-nya bisa memicu notifikasi via EventBridge.","Salah — S3 access logs hanya mencakup request S3 dan analisis mingguan bukan deteksi anomali otomatis."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'unusual volume of API calls' tanpa threshold → CloudTrail Insights."},{"id":"E1C-14","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Idempotent pipeline steps","q":"A Step Functions workflow loads daily batches into an Amazon Redshift fact table. When the load task times out and is retried, the same batch is sometimes inserted twice, causing duplicate rows. The retry behavior must be kept. Which solution will prevent duplicates?","o":["Remove all Retry configurations from the load task.","Make the load idempotent: COPY each batch into a staging table, then in one transaction delete rows in the target table that match the batch ID and insert the rows from staging (or use MERGE).","Switch the workflow to an Express workflow so each state runs at most once.","Place an Amazon SQS FIFO queue in front of the load task."],"a":[1],"e":"Syaratnya adalah mencegah duplikat sambil 'the retry behavior must be kept'. Solusinya membuat langkah load 'idempotent': hasil akhirnya sama walaupun dijalankan berkali-kali. Pola staging table + delete/insert berdasarkan batch ID dalam satu transaksi (atau MERGE di Redshift) memastikan pengulangan load mengganti data batch yang sama, bukan menambah. Distractor terdekat adalah menghapus Retry: duplikat hilang tetapi ketahanan pipeline turun, melanggar syarat. Express workflow asinkron justru bersifat at-least-once, sehingga tidak menjamin sekali eksekusi. SQS FIFO hanya mendeduplikasi pesan dalam jendela 5 menit di antrean, bukan operasi ulang ke Redshift. Aturan umum: dalam pipeline dengan retry, setiap langkah tulis harus idempotent (upsert/merge, overwrite partisi, kunci batch).","r":["Salah — Menghilangkan retry mengurangi fault tolerance dan bertentangan dengan syarat.","Benar — Staging + delete/insert atau MERGE per batch ID membuat load idempotent sehingga retry tidak menghasilkan duplikat.","Salah — Express workflow asinkron bersifat at-least-once, tidak menjamin eksekusi tunggal.","Salah — FIFO dedup hanya berlaku untuk pesan antrean dalam jendela singkat, bukan untuk COPY yang diulang."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'retry menyebabkan duplikat' → buat langkah idempotent (staging + MERGE/upsert)."},{"id":"E1C-28","d":1,"ts":"1.3.3","t":"EventBridge Pipes","q":"A DynamoDB table has DynamoDB Streams enabled. A data engineer must start an AWS Step Functions workflow only for INSERT events where the new item has status 'NEW'. Before the workflow starts, each event must be enriched with customer details returned by an existing AWS Lambda function. The solution must use the LEAST custom code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a Lambda event source mapping on the stream with a function that filters the events in code, calls the enrichment function, and then calls StartExecution.","Create an Amazon EventBridge Pipe with the DynamoDB stream as the source, an event filter for INSERT events with status 'NEW', the existing Lambda function as the enrichment step, and the state machine as the target.","Export the table to Amazon S3 every hour and start the workflow from an S3 event notification.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule on the default event bus that matches DynamoDB INSERT events."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: sumber DynamoDB Streams, 'only for INSERT events where ... status NEW', langkah 'enriched' dengan Lambda yang sudah ada, target Step Functions, dan 'LEAST custom code'. EventBridge Pipes menghubungkan sumber point-to-point (DynamoDB Streams, Kinesis, SQS, dll.) ke target dengan tahapan filter, enrichment opsional (Lambda, Step Functions Express, API Gateway, API destination), dan target, semuanya deklaratif. Distractor terdekat adalah Lambda event source mapping kustom: bisa bekerja, tetapi semua logika filter, orkestrasi enrichment, dan StartExecution menjadi kode yang harus dipelihara. DynamoDB Streams tidak mengirim event item ke default event bus, sehingga rule EventBridge biasa tidak menerimanya. Ekspor per jam melanggar sifat event-driven. Aturan umum: source → filter → enrich → target tanpa kode → EventBridge Pipes.","r":["Salah — Berfungsi, tetapi seluruh filter dan orkestrasi ditulis sebagai kode kustom.","Benar — Pipes menyediakan filter, enrichment, dan target Step Functions secara deklaratif dari DynamoDB Streams.","Salah — Ekspor terjadwal tidak real time dan tidak memfilter event INSERT.","Salah — Perubahan item DynamoDB Streams tidak dikirim ke default event bus EventBridge."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'stream/queue → filter → enrichment → target' → EventBridge Pipes."},{"id":"E1A-14","d":1,"ts":"1.1.2","t":"AWS Transfer Family","q":"Several external business partners deliver daily CSV files to a company by using SFTP. The company wants the files to land directly in an Amazon S3 bucket for downstream processing, and the partners must not change their existing SFTP clients. Which solution has the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create an AWS Transfer Family SFTP server that uses the Amazon S3 bucket as its storage backend.","Run an SFTP server on an Amazon EC2 instance and use a cron job to copy the files to Amazon S3.","Give each partner an IAM user and ask them to upload the files with the AWS CLI.","Use AWS DataSync with an SFTP location to pull the files from each partner every day."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: partner memakai 'SFTP', 'must not change their existing SFTP clients', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Transfer Family menyediakan endpoint SFTP yang fully managed dengan penyimpanan langsung di S3 (atau EFS), sehingga file mitra langsung mendarat di bucket tanpa server yang perlu dikelola. Distraktor terdekat adalah SFTP server di EC2: berfungsi, tetapi Anda harus mengelola OS, patch, high availability, dan script penyalinan. Meminta mitra memakai AWS CLI melanggar syarat tidak mengubah client. DataSync menarik data dari sistem storage yang Anda akses, sedangkan di sini mitra yang mendorong file ke perusahaan. Aturan umum: pihak eksternal mengirim file via SFTP/FTPS/AS2 ke S3 = Transfer Family.","r":["Benar — Transfer Family menyediakan SFTP managed dengan backend S3 tanpa perubahan di sisi mitra.","Salah — Server SFTP di EC2 menambah beban patching, HA, dan script penyalinan.","Salah — Mitra harus mengganti client SFTP mereka dengan AWS CLI, melanggar persyaratan.","Salah — Pola ini menarik data dari server mitra; mitra di sini mendorong file via SFTP ke perusahaan."],"k":"Partner kirim file via SFTP/FTPS/AS2 langsung ke S3 → AWS Transfer Family."},{"id":"E2C-26","d":2,"ts":"2.4.3","t":"DMS Schema Conversion extension packs","q":"During a SQL Server to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL conversion with AWS DMS Schema Conversion, several converted objects call SQL Server system functions that have no native equivalent in PostgreSQL. The team wants the converted code to work without rewriting every call. What does DMS Schema Conversion provide for this situation?","o":["An extension pack that is installed in the target database and emulates some source database functions.","An AWS Lambda layer that intercepts SQL calls at runtime.","Automatic creation of Amazon RDS Proxy to translate T-SQL to PostgreSQL.","A Babelfish cluster that DMS Schema Conversion creates automatically for every migration project."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah fungsi sumber yang 'have no native equivalent' di target dan keinginan agar kode hasil konversi tetap berjalan. DMS Schema Conversion menyediakan extension pack, yaitu schema tambahan di database target berisi fungsi dan prosedur yang mengemulasikan sebagian fitur database sumber, sehingga kode hasil konversi dapat memanggilnya. Lambda layer tidak mencegat panggilan SQL di dalam database. RDS Proxy adalah connection pooler dan tidak menerjemahkan dialek SQL. Babelfish for Aurora PostgreSQL memang dapat memahami T-SQL, tetapi itu fitur Aurora yang harus diaktifkan secara terpisah dan bukan sesuatu yang dibuat otomatis oleh DMS Schema Conversion. Aturan umum: fitur sumber yang tidak ada di target → extension pack dari DMS Schema Conversion (konsep yang sama dengan AWS SCT).","r":["Benar — Extension pack menambahkan fungsi emulasi di target agar kode hasil konversi tetap berjalan.","Salah — Lambda layer tidak berada di jalur eksekusi SQL di dalam database.","Salah — RDS Proxy hanya mengelola koneksi, bukan menerjemahkan dialek SQL.","Salah — Babelfish adalah fitur Aurora terpisah dan tidak dibuat otomatis oleh DMS Schema Conversion."],"k":"Tips ujian: fungsi sumber tanpa padanan di target → extension pack (DMS Schema Conversion)."},{"id":"E2C-21","d":2,"ts":"2.4.3","t":"Heterogeneous migration with DMS Schema Conversion and DMS","q":"A company is migrating an on-premises Oracle database (tables, views, PL/SQL packages, and triggers) to Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL. The source must stay online during migration, and cutover downtime must be minimal. The company prefers fully managed AWS capabilities over installing desktop tools. Which TWO actions should the data engineer take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Use AWS DMS Schema Conversion in a migration project to convert the schema and code objects and apply them to Aurora PostgreSQL.","Use an AWS DMS replication task with full load and change data capture (CDC) to migrate the data and keep it in sync until cutover.","Use AWS DataSync to copy the Oracle data files to Amazon S3 and attach them to Aurora PostgreSQL.","Use an AWS Glue crawler on the Oracle database to generate the PostgreSQL DDL automatically.","Use Oracle Data Pump to export the database and import the dump file into Aurora PostgreSQL."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah migrasi heterogen (Oracle ke Aurora PostgreSQL), 'source must stay online', downtime minimal, dan 'fully managed'. Migrasi heterogen membutuhkan dua bagian: konversi schema dan kode, lalu perpindahan data. AWS DMS Schema Conversion adalah fitur terkelola berbasis web di AWS DMS yang mengonversi tabel, view, stored procedure, function, dan objek lain ke dialek target, dibangun di atas engine AWS SCT tanpa perlu instalasi desktop. Setelah schema ada di target, DMS replication task dengan full load + CDC memindahkan data dan terus mereplikasi perubahan sampai cutover sehingga downtime minimal. DataSync memindahkan file, bukan mengonversi datafile Oracle menjadi tabel PostgreSQL. Glue crawler membuat metadata katalog, bukan DDL PostgreSQL beserta kode PL/SQL. Data Pump hanya kompatibel antar Oracle. Aturan umum: heterogen → DMS Schema Conversion untuk schema/kode + DMS task (full load + CDC) untuk data.","r":["Benar — DMS Schema Conversion mengonversi schema dan objek kode Oracle ke PostgreSQL secara terkelola.","Benar — Full load + CDC memindahkan data dan menjaga sinkronisasi hingga cutover dengan downtime minimal.","Salah — DataSync memindahkan file; datafile Oracle tidak bisa dipasang ke Aurora PostgreSQL.","Salah — Glue crawler hanya membuat metadata Data Catalog dan tidak mengonversi PL/SQL atau membuat DDL target.","Salah — Dump Data Pump hanya bisa diimpor ke Oracle, bukan PostgreSQL."],"k":"Tips ujian: migrasi heterogen → DMS Schema Conversion (schema/kode) + DMS full load + CDC (data)."},{"id":"E2B-38","d":2,"ts":"2.3.2","t":"S3 Lifecycle rule filters","q":"A data lake bucket contains a raw/ prefix and a curated/ prefix. Only raw objects that are tagged 'source=partner' must move to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval after 60 days; all other objects must remain in S3 Standard. The data engineer wants a solution that requires no code. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Create an S3 Lifecycle rule with a filter that combines the prefix raw/ and the object tag source=partner, with a transition to S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval after 60 days.","Create an S3 Lifecycle rule for the whole bucket that transitions all objects after 60 days, and restore curated objects when needed.","Write an AWS Lambda function that runs daily, finds tagged objects older than 60 days, and copies them to the GLACIER storage class.","Enable S3 Intelligent-Tiering with the Archive Access tier for the bucket."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'Only raw objects that are tagged source=partner', 'after 60 days' dan 'no code'. Filter S3 Lifecycle rule bisa memakai prefix, satu atau lebih object tag, dan ukuran objek, digabung dengan operator And. Rule dengan filter prefix raw/ dan tag source=partner hanya berlaku untuk objek yang tepat, lalu transisi ke Glacier Flexible Retrieval setelah 60 hari berjalan otomatis. Rule untuk seluruh bucket memindahkan data curated yang seharusnya tetap di Standard. Lambda harian berfungsi, tetapi melanggar syarat tanpa kode. Intelligent-Tiering tidak bisa dibatasi dengan aturan umur 60 hari per tag dan berlaku berdasarkan akses, bukan kriteria bisnis. Ingat: lifecycle untuk subset objek → filter prefix/tag/size.","r":["Benar — Filter prefix + tag membatasi transisi pada objek yang tepat tanpa kode.","Salah — Rule untuk seluruh bucket memindahkan objek curated yang harus tetap di Standard.","Salah — Lambda adalah kode kustom, padahal Lifecycle rule bisa melakukannya secara native.","Salah — Intelligent-Tiering bekerja berdasarkan pola akses, bukan aturan 60 hari untuk tag tertentu."],"k":"Tips ujian: lifecycle hanya untuk sebagian objek → Lifecycle rule filter (prefix, tags, object size)."},{"id":"E4B-28","d":4,"ts":"4.4.2","t":"CloudWatch Logs retention and archiving","q":"A company collects pipeline logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Engineers query the logs frequently during the first 30 days. A regulation requires that all logs be retained for 7 years, but logs older than 30 days are almost never accessed. The company wants to minimize storage cost and operational effort. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Create a subscription filter that streams the log events to Amazon Data Firehose for delivery to Amazon S3 with an S3 Lifecycle rule that transitions objects to S3 Glacier Deep Archive, and set the log group retention to 30 days.","Set the log group retention to 'Never expire' so that all logs remain in CloudWatch Logs.","Run a CloudWatch Logs export task manually at the end of each month to copy the previous month's logs to Amazon S3.","Create a new log group in the Infrequent Access log class for the pipeline logs and keep all logs there for 7 years."],"a":[0],"e":"Syaratnya: akses sering 30 hari, retensi '7 years' dengan biaya serendah mungkin dan 'operational effort' minimal. Subscription filter mengalirkan log secara otomatis dan berkelanjutan ke Amazon Data Firehose yang mengirimkannya ke S3; S3 Lifecycle memindahkan data ke Glacier Deep Archive, kelas penyimpanan termurah untuk arsip jangka panjang. Retention 30 hari pada log group menghapus salinan mahal di CloudWatch Logs setelah masa akses aktif. Distraktor terdekat adalah export task bulanan: data juga sampai ke S3, tetapi prosesnya manual dan rawan terlewat sehingga melanggar syarat effort minimal. 'Never expire' menyimpan log 7 tahun di CloudWatch Logs dengan biaya penyimpanan yang jauh lebih tinggi daripada Deep Archive. Infrequent Access log class hanya menurunkan biaya ingestion; harga storage-nya sama dengan Standard, sehingga menyimpan 7 tahun di sana tetap jauh lebih mahal daripada Deep Archive (log class juga tidak bisa diubah setelah log group dibuat). Aturan umum: log jangka panjang murah → stream/export ke S3 + lifecycle ke Glacier, retention pendek di CloudWatch Logs.","r":["Benar — Pengiriman otomatis ke S3 + lifecycle ke Deep Archive menekan biaya, dan retention 30 hari menjaga akses cepat untuk data baru.","Salah — Menyimpan 7 tahun di CloudWatch Logs jauh lebih mahal daripada arsip di S3 Glacier Deep Archive.","Salah — Export manual bulanan menambah effort operasional dan risiko kelupaan.","Salah — Infrequent Access hanya lebih murah di ingestion; biaya storage sama dengan Standard sehingga retensi 7 tahun tetap jauh lebih mahal daripada Glacier Deep Archive."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'retain logs for years cheaply' → CloudWatch Logs → (subscription filter/Firehose) S3 → Glacier Deep Archive + retention pendek."},{"id":"E1C-03","d":1,"ts":"1.3.1","t":"AWS Glue workflow conditional triggers","q":"A data team uses only AWS Glue. A pipeline contains Glue job A (load customers) and Glue job B (load orders) that can run in parallel, followed by Glue job C (join and aggregate), which must start only after BOTH A and B succeed. The team wants to monitor the whole pipeline as one run in the AWS Glue console and share parameters between the jobs. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST effort?","o":["Create an AWS Glue workflow with a start trigger for jobs A and B, and a conditional trigger that watches jobs A and B with the logical condition ALL and state SUCCEEDED to start job C.","Create an AWS Glue workflow with a conditional trigger that watches jobs A and B with the logical condition ANY and state SUCCEEDED to start job C.","Schedule jobs A and B at 01:00 and schedule job C at 03:00 by using separate scheduled triggers.","Create two Amazon EventBridge rules that each start job C when job A or job B changes to the SUCCEEDED state."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhan kunci: job C jalan hanya jika 'BOTH A and B succeed', dipantau sebagai 'one run in the AWS Glue console', dan berbagi parameter. Glue workflow dengan conditional trigger berlogika ALL (AND) memenuhi dependensi tersebut, menampilkan graf run tunggal, dan mendukung workflow run properties untuk berbagi parameter antar job. Distractor terdekat adalah kondisi ANY: job C akan jalan begitu salah satu job selesai, sehingga bisa memproses data orders yang belum lengkap. Jadwal berbasis offset waktu rapuh karena tidak menjamin A dan B sudah selesai pada jam 03:00. Dua aturan EventBridge akan memicu job C dua kali dan tidak memeriksa kedua job sekaligus. Aturan umum: dependensi fan-in di Glue → conditional trigger dengan logical ALL.","r":["Benar — Conditional trigger dengan ALL + SUCCEEDED memastikan C menunggu A dan B, dan workflow memberi tampilan run tunggal serta run properties.","Salah — Logika ANY memicu C saat salah satu job selesai, sehingga input C bisa belum lengkap.","Salah — Offset waktu tidak menjamin dependensi; jika A atau B terlambat, C membaca data parsial.","Salah — Dua rule memicu C dua kali dan tidak ada pemeriksaan bahwa kedua job sudah sukses; juga tidak terlihat sebagai satu workflow run."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue fan-in 'both jobs succeed' → conditional trigger Logical = ALL (bukan ANY)."},{"id":"E4B-03","d":4,"ts":"4.3.1","t":"DataBrew PII pseudonymization","q":"A marketing analytics team with no programming experience prepares datasets in AWS Glue DataBrew. Company policy states that customer_id values must not be visible in shared datasets. However, analysts must still be able to join several pseudonymized datasets on customer_id. Which DataBrew approach meets these requirements?","o":["Apply a hashing transformation to customer_id in every dataset using the same secret key so the same input always produces the same pseudonymized value.","Apply a random character masking transformation to customer_id so each value is replaced with random characters.","Remove the customer_id column from all datasets before they are shared.","Store the datasets in Amazon S3 with SSE-KMS so customer_id is encrypted at rest."],"a":[0],"e":"Ada dua constraint yang harus dipenuhi bersamaan: customer_id 'must not be visible' dan analis tetap 'able to join ... on customer_id', ditambah tim tanpa kemampuan coding. DataBrew menyediakan recipe step no-code untuk PII seperti hashing (dengan secret yang sama) dan deterministic encryption. Hash dengan secret yang sama bersifat deterministik: input yang sama selalu menghasilkan output yang sama, sehingga join antar dataset tetap berfungsi tetapi nilai asli tidak terlihat. Distraktor terdekat adalah random masking: nilai memang tersembunyi, tetapi hasil acak berbeda untuk input yang sama sehingga join rusak. Menghapus kolom membuat join mustahil. SSE-KMS hanya mengenkripsi saat disimpan; pengguna yang membaca dataset tetap melihat customer_id asli. Aturan umum: pseudonimisasi yang tetap bisa di-join → transformasi deterministik (hash/deterministic encryption), bukan masking acak.","r":["Benar — Hash deterministik menyembunyikan nilai asli namun tetap konsisten sehingga join antar dataset berfungsi, dan bisa dilakukan no-code di DataBrew.","Salah — Masking acak menghasilkan nilai berbeda untuk ID yang sama sehingga join antar dataset tidak lagi mungkin.","Salah — Tanpa kolom customer_id, dataset tidak dapat di-join sama sekali.","Salah — Enkripsi at rest transparan bagi pembaca berizin; customer_id tetap terlihat di dataset."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'hide identifier but keep joins working' → deterministic hashing/deterministic encryption; random masking merusak join."},{"id":"E1C-51","d":1,"ts":"1.4.2","t":"Lambda memory and CPU allocation","q":"An AWS Lambda function configured with 512 MB of memory decompresses and parses large JSON files. CloudWatch metrics show that the function uses only 300 MB of memory, but its duration is long and the code is CPU-bound and multithreaded. Which change will MOST likely reduce the function's duration?","o":["Reduce the memory to 320 MB because the function does not use all of its memory.","Increase the function's ephemeral storage (/tmp) to 10 GB.","Configure provisioned concurrency for the function.","Increase the memory setting, because Lambda allocates CPU power in proportion to the configured memory."],"a":[3],"e":"Petunjuk kuncinya: kode 'CPU-bound and multithreaded' dan memori yang terpakai hanya 300 MB. Di Lambda, memori (128 MB hingga 10.240 MB) adalah satu-satunya pengaturan kinerja komputasi: CPU dialokasikan proporsional terhadap memori (pada 1.769 MB setara satu vCPU, dan bertambah seiring memori). Menaikkan memori memberi lebih banyak CPU sehingga durasi pekerjaan CPU-bound turun, dan sering kali total biaya tidak naik banyak karena durasi lebih pendek. Distractor terdekat adalah menurunkan memori karena tidak terpakai: logis bila hanya melihat RAM, tetapi justru memangkas CPU dan memperlambat fungsi. Ephemeral storage tidak menambah CPU. Provisioned concurrency hanya mengurangi cold start. Aturan umum: fungsi Lambda CPU-bound lambat → naikkan memori (CPU ikut naik).","r":["Salah — Mengurangi memori juga mengurangi CPU sehingga fungsi lebih lambat.","Salah — /tmp yang lebih besar tidak menambah daya komputasi.","Salah — Provisioned concurrency tidak mempercepat eksekusi setelah inisialisasi.","Benar — Memori lebih tinggi memberi CPU lebih banyak, mempercepat beban kerja CPU-bound."],"k":"Tips ujian: Lambda CPU-bound → tambah memory (CPU dialokasikan proporsional terhadap memori)."},{"id":"E3A-61","d":3,"ts":"3.2.5","t":"EMR on EC2 vs EMR Serverless","q":"A company runs about 40 Apache Spark jobs per day. The jobs start at unpredictable times, vary widely in size, and each runs for 5 to 30 minutes. A long-running Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster sized for the largest job is idle most of the day. The team does not want to manage cluster sizing, instances, or scaling policies, and the jobs must keep using the same Spark code. Which solution meets these requirements MOST cost-effectively?","o":["Keep the EMR on EC2 cluster and purchase Reserved Instances for all nodes.","Move the jobs to Amazon EMR Serverless and submit each job to an EMR Serverless application that scales workers per job.","Rewrite the jobs as AWS Lambda functions.","Move the jobs to an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster and rewrite them in SQL."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'unpredictable times', 'vary widely in size', 'cluster idle most of the day', 'not manage cluster sizing', dan 'same Spark code'. Amazon EMR Serverless menjalankan job Spark tanpa cluster yang harus dikelola; kapasitas worker disediakan dan dilepas otomatis per job, dan tagihan hanya untuk vCPU, memori, dan storage yang dipakai selama job berjalan. Kode Spark yang sama tetap bisa dipakai. Reserved Instances untuk cluster yang idle sebagian besar waktu tetap membayar kapasitas yang tidak terpakai. Lambda punya batas 15 menit dan tidak menjalankan Spark, sehingga perlu menulis ulang kode. Redshift memerlukan penulisan ulang ke SQL dan cluster provisioned juga idle. Trade-off-nya: EMR on EC2 memberi kontrol penuh (tipe instance, Spot, konfigurasi) dan bisa lebih murah untuk utilisasi tinggi yang stabil, sedangkan EMR Serverless unggul untuk beban yang bervariasi dan sporadis. Aturan umum: Spark sporadis tanpa kelola cluster → EMR Serverless.","r":["Salah — Reserved Instances tetap membayar kapasitas yang sebagian besar idle.","Benar — EMR Serverless menyediakan kapasitas per job dan menagih hanya saat job berjalan, dengan kode Spark yang sama.","Salah — Lambda tidak menjalankan Spark, dibatasi 15 menit, dan menuntut penulisan ulang kode.","Salah — Membutuhkan penulisan ulang ke SQL dan cluster provisioned juga akan idle."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Spark jobs, variable/unpredictable, no cluster management' → EMR Serverless; 'steady high utilization + full control' → EMR on EC2."},{"id":"E2C-15","d":2,"ts":"2.4.2","t":"Iceberg partition evolution","q":"An Apache Iceberg table in Amazon S3 is partitioned by day(event_ts). Event volume has grown 40 times, and queries now target hourly windows. The data engineer wants new data to be partitioned by hour without rewriting the existing 2 years of daily-partitioned data, and analysts must not have to change their queries. Which approach meets these requirements?","o":["Create a new table partitioned by hour, copy all historical data into it, and drop the old table.","Use Iceberg partition evolution from an Apache Spark job on AWS Glue to replace the day(event_ts) partition field with hour(event_ts).","Add a new string column named event_hour and require analysts to filter on it.","Run an AWS Glue crawler with a new partition index on event_ts."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'without rewriting the existing data' dan 'analysts must not have to change their queries'. Iceberg mendukung partition evolution: spesifikasi partisi bisa diubah (misalnya dari day ke hour) dan hanya data baru yang ditulis dengan spesifikasi baru, sementara data lama tetap dengan spesifikasi lama. Karena Iceberg memakai hidden partitioning, analis tetap memfilter pada event_ts dan Iceberg otomatis melakukan pruning di kedua spesifikasi. Perubahan ini dilakukan dengan DDL Spark (Iceberg SQL extensions) seperti ALTER TABLE ... REPLACE PARTITION FIELD yang dijalankan di AWS Glue atau Amazon EMR; Athena sendiri mendukung DDL schema evolution untuk Iceberg tetapi belum menyediakan DDL partition evolution. Membuat tabel baru dan menyalin seluruh data historis melanggar syarat tanpa rewrite. Kolom event_hour baru memaksa analis mengubah query. Partition index crawler hanya mempercepat lookup partisi tabel Hive, bukan mengubah skema partisi Iceberg. Aturan umum: ubah granularitas partisi tanpa rewrite → Iceberg partition evolution + hidden partitioning.","r":["Salah — Menyalin seluruh data historis ke tabel baru adalah rewrite penuh yang ingin dihindari.","Benar — Partition evolution Iceberg mengubah spesifikasi untuk data baru saja, dan hidden partitioning membuat query tetap sama.","Salah — Kolom partisi eksplisit baru memaksa analis mengubah filter query mereka.","Salah — Partition index pada Glue Data Catalog tidak mengubah spesifikasi partisi tabel Iceberg."],"k":"Tips ujian: ganti granularitas partisi tanpa rewrite data dan tanpa ubah query → Iceberg partition evolution (hidden partitioning)."},{"id":"E2B-27","d":2,"ts":"2.2.6","t":"SageMaker Catalog AI-generated metadata","q":"A data platform team must add business context to 800 newly onboarded tables in Amazon SageMaker Catalog. Most tables have no descriptions, and the data stewards have limited time. The team wants to reduce manual documentation effort while keeping a human review step before assets become discoverable. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler again with a custom classifier that writes descriptions to the table parameters.","Ask each data steward to write table and column descriptions manually in the Glue console.","Use the AI-generated description recommendations in SageMaker Catalog, have stewards review and accept or edit them, and then publish the assets.","Publish all 800 tables immediately without descriptions and rely on analysts to add comments later."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: '800 ... tables', 'limited time', 'reduce manual documentation effort' dan 'keeping a human review step'. SageMaker Catalog dapat membuat rekomendasi deskripsi bisnis (ringkasan tabel, use case, deskripsi kolom) dengan model generatif di Amazon Bedrock. Steward meninjau, menerima atau mengedit rekomendasi, lalu mempublikasikan asset, sehingga ada review manusia sebelum asset dapat ditemukan. Menulis manual di Glue console tidak mengurangi pekerjaan dan hanya mengisi technical catalog. Crawler dan classifier menyimpulkan skema, bukan deskripsi bisnis. Publish tanpa deskripsi melanggar tujuan discoverability dan tidak ada review. Ingat: 'automate business descriptions' di business catalog → AI recommendations di SageMaker Catalog, dengan review sebelum publish.","r":["Salah — Crawler dan classifier menyimpulkan skema teknis, bukan deskripsi bisnis.","Salah — Dokumentasi manual 800 tabel tidak mengurangi beban steward dan tidak memakai business catalog.","Benar — Rekomendasi deskripsi berbasis AI mengurangi pekerjaan manual, dan steward tetap meninjau sebelum publish.","Salah — Publish tanpa konteks bisnis melewati review dan membuat data sulit dipahami."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'generate business descriptions automatically' + 'review' → AI recommendations di SageMaker Catalog."},{"id":"E2A-03","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"Redshift for OLAP workloads","q":"A company's analytics team needs to run complex SQL queries with multi-table joins and aggregations over 60 TB of structured sales history. More than 200 business users access the data through BI dashboards throughout the day, and the dashboards must return results in seconds. Which data store should a data engineer choose?","o":["Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL with the largest available instance class and several read replicas","Amazon Redshift with RA3 nodes","Amazon DynamoDB tables with global secondary indexes for each report dimension","CSV files in Amazon S3 queried with Amazon Athena"],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhan yang menentukan adalah 'complex SQL queries with multi-table joins and aggregations', volume '60 TB', dan banyak pengguna BI yang butuh hasil dalam hitungan detik. Ini adalah workload OLAP klasik, dan Amazon Redshift dirancang untuk itu dengan columnar storage, MPP (massively parallel processing), dan result caching. Node RA3 memisahkan compute dan managed storage sehingga 60 TB bisa disimpan secara efisien. Distraktor terdekat adalah RDS for PostgreSQL: ia mendukung SQL dan join, tetapi engine row-based OLTP tidak efisien untuk agregasi besar di puluhan TB. Athena atas CSV harus memindai file teks mentah sehingga lambat dan mahal untuk dashboard konkuren. DynamoDB tidak mendukung join dan agregasi ad-hoc. Aturan umum: analitik SQL kompleks skala TB–PB dengan banyak user BI → Amazon Redshift.","r":["Salah — RDS adalah database OLTP row-based; agregasi pada 60 TB akan lambat dan sulit diskalakan meskipun memakai read replica.","Benar — Redshift adalah data warehouse columnar MPP yang dioptimalkan untuk join dan agregasi kompleks dengan konkurensi BI.","Salah — DynamoDB adalah key-value store tanpa join dan agregasi SQL; membuat GSI per dimensi tidak menggantikan kemampuan OLAP.","Salah — Athena atas CSV memindai seluruh data teks tanpa kompresi kolumnar, sehingga dashboard lambat dan biaya per query tinggi."],"k":"Complex joins + aggregations + TB-scale + BI concurrency → Amazon Redshift."},{"id":"E4A-51","d":4,"ts":"4.2.5","t":"ABAC with principal and resource tags","q":"A company tags every Amazon S3 data lake object prefix and AWS Glue job with a project tag. Each data engineer's IAM role is also tagged with project. The company wants one IAM policy that allows engineers to start only the Glue jobs that belong to their own project, without updating the policy when new projects are created. Which policy condition meets this requirement?","o":["\"StringEquals\": {\"aws:RequestedRegion\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/project}\"}","\"StringLike\": {\"aws:PrincipalArn\": \"arn:aws:iam::*:role/project-*\"}","\"StringEquals\": {\"aws:ResourceTag/project\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/project}\"}","\"StringEquals\": {\"aws:ResourceTag/project\": \"analytics\"}"],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'only ... their own project' dan 'without updating the policy when new projects are created'. Attribute-based access control (ABAC) membandingkan tag pada principal dengan tag pada resource di dalam satu policy. Kondisi aws:ResourceTag/project sama dengan ${aws:PrincipalTag/project} berarti engineer hanya dapat bertindak pada resource yang tag project-nya sama dengan tag pada role mereka, dan project baru cukup ditangani dengan memberi tag. Nilai tetap seperti 'analytics' adalah pendekatan per project yang membutuhkan policy baru untuk setiap project. Pola nama ARN role tidak menghubungkan engineer dengan resource project-nya. aws:RequestedRegion mengatur Region, bukan kepemilikan project. Aturan umum: ABAC = aws:ResourceTag/key dibandingkan dengan ${aws:PrincipalTag/key}.","r":["Salah — Kondisi Region tidak ada hubungannya dengan kepemilikan project.","Salah — Pola nama role tidak membatasi resource mana yang boleh diakses.","Benar — Mencocokkan tag resource dengan tag principal adalah inti ABAC dan otomatis berlaku untuk project baru.","Salah — Nilai statis hanya berlaku untuk satu project dan perlu policy baru untuk setiap project."],"k":"Tips ujian: ABAC → \"aws:ResourceTag/X\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/X}\"; skala tanpa update policy."},{"id":"E4A-04","d":4,"ts":"4.1.1","t":"Security groups vs network ACLs","q":"A data platform runs an Amazon EMR cluster in a private subnet. The security groups attached to the cluster allow HTTPS traffic from a partner CIDR range 198.51.100.0/22. The security team detects malicious traffic from 198.51.101.0/24, which is inside the partner range, and must block only that /24 immediately without affecting the rest of the partner range. Which solution meets this requirement?","o":["Add a deny rule for 198.51.101.0/24 to the EMR security groups with a higher priority than the allow rule.","Add an inbound deny rule for 198.51.101.0/24 to the subnet's network ACL with a lower rule number than any allow rules.","Remove the partner CIDR rule from the EMR security groups and add AWS WAF in front of the EMR cluster.","Replace the partner CIDR rule with a rule that references the partner's security group ID."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'block only that /24' di dalam rentang yang sudah diizinkan. Security group hanya mendukung rule allow; tidak ada rule deny dan tidak ada prioritas, sehingga tidak bisa mengecualikan sebagian rentang dari rule allow yang lebih luas. Network ACL mendukung rule allow dan deny yang dievaluasi berurutan dari rule number terkecil, sehingga deny untuk /24 dengan nomor lebih kecil akan diproses sebelum allow. AWS WAF tidak bisa dipasang langsung ke EMR; WAF hanya untuk CloudFront, ALB, API Gateway, dan sejenisnya. Mereferensikan security group partner hanya mungkin dalam VPC yang sama atau peering, dan tidak menyelesaikan pemblokiran sebagian traffic. Aturan umum: perlu 'deny' eksplisit untuk IP tertentu → network ACL, bukan security group.","r":["Salah — Security group tidak mendukung deny rule maupun prioritas rule.","Benar — Network ACL mendukung deny eksplisit yang dievaluasi berdasarkan urutan rule number, sehingga /24 tersebut terblokir tanpa mengganggu sisa rentang partner.","Salah — WAF tidak dapat dipasang di depan EMR cluster secara langsung, dan menghapus rule partner memutus seluruh partner.","Salah — Referensi security group lintas jaringan partner tidak dimungkinkan dan tidak memblokir subnet tertentu."],"k":"Tips ujian: security group = allow-only dan stateful; network ACL = allow + deny, stateless, berurutan menurut rule number."},{"id":"E1B-26","d":1,"ts":"1.2.3","t":"Aurora zero-ETL integration with Redshift","q":"A company wants to analyze transactional data from an Amazon Aurora MySQL database together with other data in Amazon Redshift. The analytics team needs the Aurora data to be available in Redshift within seconds of each change. The company wants to avoid building and maintaining any custom ETL or replication pipelines. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure an Amazon Aurora zero-ETL integration with Amazon Redshift.","Create an AWS Glue ETL job that runs every 5 minutes with job bookmarks to copy new rows into Redshift.","Configure AWS DMS with change data capture from Aurora MySQL to Redshift on a replication instance.","Export Aurora snapshots to Amazon S3 every hour and query them with Redshift Spectrum."],"a":[0],"e":"Frasa penentunya adalah 'within seconds of each change' dan 'avoid building and maintaining any custom ETL or replication pipelines'. Aurora zero-ETL integration dengan Redshift mereplikasi data transaksional secara near-real-time ke Redshift tanpa pipeline yang harus Anda bangun atau kelola. DMS dengan CDC adalah distraktor terdekat karena juga near-real-time, tetapi Anda harus mengelola replication instance, task, dan mapping, sehingga overhead lebih tinggi. Glue tiap 5 menit tidak mencapai latensi detik dan merupakan pipeline kustom. Snapshot export per jam terlalu lambat. Aturan umum: Aurora/RDS → Redshift near-real-time tanpa pipeline → zero-ETL integration.","r":["Benar — Zero-ETL mereplikasi perubahan Aurora ke Redshift dalam hitungan detik tanpa pipeline kustom.","Salah — Glue tiap 5 menit tidak memenuhi latensi detik dan merupakan pipeline yang harus dikelola.","Salah — DMS CDC berfungsi, tetapi membutuhkan replication instance dan task yang harus dikelola.","Salah — Snapshot per jam jauh dari latensi detik."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Aurora → Redshift + near real time + no ETL pipeline' → zero-ETL integration."},{"id":"E4A-43","d":4,"ts":"4.2.3","t":"Database roles and IAM DB authentication","q":"An Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL database supports a reporting application and an ETL process. Currently both use the master user. The security team wants the reporting application to have read-only access to the reporting schema and wants the ETL process to authenticate with its IAM role instead of a password. Which TWO actions meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Grant the rds_superuser role to the reporting application's database user.","Create a database role with USAGE on the reporting schema and SELECT on its tables, and grant that role to the reporting application's database user.","Attach an IAM policy to the reporting application's role that allows rds:* on the DB cluster to limit table access.","Keep the ETL process on the master user and store the master password in AWS Secrets Manager.","Create a database user for the ETL process, grant it the rds_iam role and the required table privileges, and allow rds-db:connect for that user in the ETL IAM role's policy."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Kata kunci: 'read-only access to the reporting schema' dan ETL 'authenticate with its IAM role instead of a password'. Hak akses di dalam database PostgreSQL diatur dengan role dan GRANT database, sehingga role read-only dengan USAGE dan SELECT yang di-grant ke user aplikasi reporting memenuhi least privilege. Untuk IAM database authentication di Aurora PostgreSQL, user database harus diberi role rds_iam, dan IAM role ETL harus punya izin rds-db:connect untuk resource dbuser tersebut; user tetap butuh GRANT tabel seperlunya. rds_superuser memberi hak administratif. IAM policy rds:* mengatur API manajemen RDS, bukan hak baca tabel. Tetap memakai master user melanggar kedua kebutuhan. Aturan umum: hak di dalam database = GRANT database; login dengan IAM = rds_iam + rds-db:connect.","r":["Salah — rds_superuser memberi hak administratif yang jauh melebihi read-only.","Benar — Role database dengan USAGE dan SELECT memberi akses read-only yang tepat ke schema reporting.","Salah — rds:* adalah API manajemen RDS dan tidak membatasi akses tabel di dalam database.","Salah — Master user melanggar least privilege dan tetap memakai password.","Benar — rds_iam plus izin rds-db:connect memungkinkan ETL login dengan token IAM, dan grant tabel membatasi aksesnya."],"k":"Tips ujian: IAM DB auth PostgreSQL → GRANT rds_iam TO user + rds-db:connect; hak tabel tetap via GRANT database."},{"id":"E1A-60","d":1,"ts":"1.1.10","t":"Cross-account log fan-in","q":"A company has 50 AWS accounts. Application logs from Amazon CloudWatch Logs in every account must be centralized in near real time into a single Amazon Kinesis data stream in a central logging account for further processing. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Deploy a Lambda function in each account that polls CloudWatch Logs every minute and writes to the central stream.","Export the logs from each account to Amazon S3 every day and copy them to the central account.","In the central account, create a CloudWatch Logs destination that points to the Kinesis data stream with an access policy allowing the 50 accounts, and create subscription filters in each source account that send logs to that destination.","Install the Kinesis Agent on every Amazon EC2 instance in all accounts."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: log dari '50 AWS accounts', 'near real time', ke 'single Kinesis data stream' di akun pusat, dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Ini adalah pola fan-in. CloudWatch Logs mendukung cross-account log data sharing: di akun pusat dibuat destination yang mengarah ke Kinesis Data Streams (atau Firehose) dengan access policy yang mengizinkan akun sumber, lalu setiap akun sumber membuat subscription filter yang mengirim log ke destination tersebut secara streaming. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda polling di setiap akun: berfungsi, tetapi berupa kode kustom di 50 akun. Export harian ke S3 tidak near real time. Kinesis Agent hanya mencakup EC2, bukan semua sumber log di CloudWatch Logs, dan butuh pengelolaan agen. Aturan umum: memusatkan log lintas akun secara streaming = CloudWatch Logs destination + subscription filter.","r":["Salah — Polling dengan Lambda di 50 akun adalah kode kustom dengan overhead tinggi.","Salah — Export harian tidak memenuhi kebutuhan near real time.","Benar — Destination lintas akun + subscription filter mengalirkan log dari banyak akun ke satu stream secara near real time.","Salah — Kinesis Agent hanya untuk EC2 dan memerlukan pengelolaan agen di semua instance."],"k":"Fan-in log lintas akun → CloudWatch Logs destination (KDS/Firehose) + subscription filter."},{"id":"E3B-52","d":3,"ts":"3.4.2","t":"DQDL CustomSql","q":"In a shipments dataset processed by AWS Glue, a business rule states that ship_date must never be earlier than order_date. No built-in single-column rule expresses this relationship. Which DQDL rule should a data engineer use?","o":["ColumnValues \"ship_date\" > \"2020-01-01\"","IsComplete \"ship_date\"","DataFreshness \"ship_date\" <= 24 hours","CustomSql \"select count(*) from primary where ship_date < order_date\" = 0"],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah hubungan antar kolom 'ship_date must never be earlier than order_date' yang tidak bisa diekspresikan dengan rule satu kolom. Rule CustomSql di DQDL menjalankan query SQL terhadap dataset (dirujuk sebagai 'primary') dan membandingkan hasilnya dengan nilai yang diharapkan; menghitung baris pelanggar lalu mensyaratkan = 0 menegakkan aturan bisnis tersebut. Distraktor terdekat adalah ColumnValues dengan tanggal tetap: hanya memeriksa rentang satu kolom, tidak membandingkan dengan order_date. IsComplete memeriksa kekosongan, dan DataFreshness memeriksa kesegaran data. Aturan: aturan bisnis lintas kolom → CustomSql.","r":["Salah — Hanya memeriksa satu kolom terhadap tanggal tetap, bukan terhadap order_date.","Salah — Kelengkapan kolom tidak menjamin urutan tanggal yang benar.","Salah — DataFreshness mengukur seberapa baru data, bukan hubungan antar kolom.","Benar — CustomSql menghitung baris yang melanggar aturan lintas kolom dan mensyaratkan hasilnya nol."],"k":"Tips ujian: aturan bisnis kompleks/lintas kolom di Glue DQ → CustomSql."},{"id":"E1B-49","d":1,"ts":"1.2.7","t":"Troubleshooting Glue job bookmarks","q":"A data engineer enabled job bookmarks on an AWS Glue ETL job that reads new files from Amazon S3 and writes to a curated prefix. However, every run still reprocesses all files, creating duplicates in the output. The job script creates the source DynamicFrame with from_catalog and ends after writing the output. What is the MOST likely cause?","o":["The S3 bucket does not have versioning enabled.","The job uses the G.1X worker type instead of G.2X.","The source read does not specify a transformation_ctx and/or the script does not call job.commit() at the end of the run.","The Glue crawler has not been run since the bookmark was enabled."],"a":[2],"e":"Petunjuk kuncinya adalah bookmark sudah diaktifkan tetapi 'every run still reprocesses all files', dan skrip 'ends after writing the output'. Agar bookmark bekerja, setiap source harus memiliki parameter transformation_ctx sebagai kunci state, dan skrip harus memanggil job.init() di awal serta job.commit() di akhir untuk menyimpan state bookmark; tanpa itu, Glue tidak mencatat file yang sudah diproses. Versioning S3 tidak diperlukan oleh bookmark. Tipe worker tidak berpengaruh pada state bookmark. Crawler hanya memperbarui metadata katalog dan tidak menyimpan posisi pemrosesan. Aturan umum: bookmark 'tidak jalan' → periksa transformation_ctx, job.init/job.commit, dan bahwa bookmark diaktifkan pada job.","r":["Salah — Bookmark tidak bergantung pada versioning S3.","Salah — Jenis worker tidak memengaruhi penyimpanan state bookmark.","Benar — Tanpa transformation_ctx dan job.commit(), state bookmark tidak tersimpan sehingga semua file dibaca ulang.","Salah — Crawler memperbarui metadata, bukan state bookmark."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'bookmarks enabled but data reprocessed' → transformation_ctx hilang atau job.commit() tidak dipanggil."},{"id":"E3B-36","d":3,"ts":"3.3.6","t":"Troubleshooting EMR Spark memory errors","q":"A Spark job on an Amazon EMR on EC2 cluster fails repeatedly with the error 'Container killed by YARN for exceeding memory limits'. The executors use 5 cores each, and the job performs wide aggregations. The cluster has plenty of free nodes. Which TWO changes will MOST likely resolve the error? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Increase spark.executor.memoryOverhead (or spark.executor.memory) for the job.","Reduce spark.executor.cores so that each executor runs fewer concurrent tasks and needs less memory.","Add more core nodes to the cluster.","Increase spark.driver.memory only.","Enable termination protection on the cluster."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Gejalanya adalah container executor dibunuh YARN karena melebihi batas memori per container — bukan karena kekurangan node ('plenty of free nodes'). Menaikkan spark.executor.memoryOverhead (memori off-heap) atau spark.executor.memory memperbesar alokasi tiap container. Mengurangi spark.executor.cores mengurangi jumlah task paralel per executor, sehingga kebutuhan memori per executor turun. Distraktor terdekat adalah menambah core node: memberi lebih banyak container, tetapi batas memori tiap container tetap sama sehingga error berulang. Menaikkan memori driver tidak membantu karena yang mati adalah container executor. Aturan: 'killed by YARN for exceeding memory limits' → atur memoryOverhead/memory dan cores per executor.","r":["Benar — Memori atau overhead executor yang lebih besar menaikkan batas memori container.","Benar — Lebih sedikit core per executor berarti lebih sedikit task bersamaan dan kebutuhan memori lebih kecil.","Salah — Node tambahan tidak mengubah batas memori setiap container executor.","Salah — Error terjadi pada container executor, bukan driver.","Salah — Termination protection tidak berhubungan dengan memori container."],"k":"Tips ujian: EMR 'Container killed by YARN for exceeding memory limits' → naikkan memoryOverhead / kurangi executor cores."},{"id":"E2A-26","d":2,"ts":"2.1.3","t":"Aurora PostgreSQL pgvector HNSW","q":"An ecommerce company stores its product catalog in Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL. The company is adding semantic product search for a generative AI assistant. Each product will have a 1,024-dimension embedding. Queries must combine vector similarity with SQL filters on price and stock status, return results with low latency and high recall, and add the LEAST operational overhead. What should a data engineer do?","o":["Export the catalog nightly to a new Amazon OpenSearch Service domain and run k-NN queries there.","Store the embeddings as JSON text columns and compute cosine similarity with a SQL function at query time.","Enable the pgvector extension in Aurora PostgreSQL, store embeddings in a vector column, and create an HNSW index on that column.","Store the embeddings in Amazon DynamoDB and use a Scan to compare vectors."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah data sudah berada di 'Aurora PostgreSQL', kebutuhan menggabungkan similarity search dengan 'SQL filters on price and stock status', 'low latency and high recall', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Ekstensi pgvector di Aurora PostgreSQL menambahkan tipe data vector dan operator jarak, dan index HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small Worlds) memberi approximate nearest neighbor search dengan latensi rendah dan recall tinggi. Karena embedding tinggal di tabel yang sama, query dapat memakai WHERE pada harga dan stok tanpa sinkronisasi ke sistem lain. Distraktor terdekat adalah OpenSearch: mendukung k-NN dengan baik, tetapi menambah domain baru, pipeline sinkronisasi, dan data menjadi basi sampai ekspor berikutnya. Menghitung cosine similarity tanpa index berarti pemindaian penuh yang lambat. Aturan umum: data relasional sudah di Aurora/RDS PostgreSQL + perlu vector search → pgvector dengan index HNSW.","r":["Salah — Domain OpenSearch terpisah dan ekspor harian menambah overhead serta membuat hasil tidak mutakhir.","Salah — Tanpa tipe vector dan index, setiap query menghitung jarak ke semua baris sehingga latensinya tinggi.","Benar — pgvector dengan index HNSW memberi similarity search cepat dengan recall tinggi dan dapat digabung dengan filter SQL di database yang sama.","Salah — DynamoDB tidak memiliki vector search native; Scan membandingkan semua item dengan biaya dan latensi tinggi."],"k":"Vector search di atas data relasional Aurora PostgreSQL → pgvector + HNSW index."},{"id":"E4B-38","d":4,"ts":"4.4.5","t":"EMR for large-scale log processing","q":"An online gaming company generates about 50 TB of clickstream and server log files per day in Amazon S3. Every night, the data engineering team must sessionize the events, join them with player reference data, and produce aggregated Parquet tables for analysis. The team has strong Apache Spark skills, and the job must be cost-effective. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Run CloudWatch Logs Insights queries on the log files every night.","Trigger an AWS Lambda function for each new log file to sessionize the events.","Index all log files in Amazon OpenSearch Service and run aggregation queries every night.","Run a nightly transient Amazon EMR cluster that uses Apache Spark, with Spot Instances for task nodes, to process the logs and write partitioned Parquet output to Amazon S3."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: volume '50 TB ... per day', proses kompleks (sessionization dan join dengan data referensi), tim dengan 'strong Apache Spark skills', dan 'cost-effective'. Amazon EMR dirancang untuk pemrosesan log bervolume sangat besar dengan Spark; cluster transient yang hanya berjalan saat job malam dan Spot Instances pada task node menekan biaya secara signifikan. Output Parquet berpartisi di S3 memudahkan analisis berikutnya. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda per file: Lambda punya batas waktu 15 menit dan memori, serta tidak cocok untuk sessionization yang membutuhkan event lintas banyak file. Logs Insights hanya bekerja pada data di CloudWatch Logs dan bukan untuk join kompleks. Mengindeks 50 TB per hari ke OpenSearch sangat mahal dan tidak ditujukan untuk transformasi batch. Aturan umum: log volume sangat besar + transformasi kompleks + skill Spark → EMR (transient + Spot).","r":["Salah — Logs Insights tidak memproses file di S3 dan tidak dirancang untuk join/sessionization skala besar.","Salah — Lambda dibatasi waktu dan memori serta tidak bisa sessionize event yang tersebar di banyak file.","Salah — Mengindeks 50 TB/hari di OpenSearch sangat mahal dan bukan untuk transformasi batch.","Benar — EMR transient dengan Spark dan Spot Instances memproses volume besar secara hemat biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'large volumes of log data + complex processing' → Amazon EMR (Spark), transient + Spot untuk hemat."},{"id":"E3A-03","d":3,"ts":"3.1.1","t":"Step Functions Distributed Map","q":"A data engineer must process 3 million small JSON files stored under one Amazon S3 prefix. Each file must be validated and transformed by an existing AWS Lambda function. The job must run with thousands of parallel invocations, record which items failed, and still succeed if fewer than 2% of the items fail. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","o":["Use an AWS Step Functions Inline Map state that iterates over a list of object keys returned by a Lambda function.","Write a Lambda function that lists the objects and invokes the processing function asynchronously in a loop.","Send every object key to an Amazon SQS queue and configure the processing Lambda function with an SQS event source mapping.","Use an AWS Step Functions Distributed Map state with an S3 item reader, invoke the Lambda function for each item, and set a tolerated failure percentage of 2%."],"a":[3],"e":"Persyaratan penentunya adalah 'millions of S3 objects', 'thousands of parallel invocations', mencatat item gagal, dan 'succeed if fewer than 2% fail'. Distributed Map di Step Functions dirancang untuk pemrosesan paralel skala besar: ia bisa membaca daftar objek langsung dari S3 (item reader), menjalankan child workflow dengan concurrency hingga ribuan, dan menulis hasil/kegagalan ke S3 (ResultWriter). Opsi ToleratedFailurePercentage membuat Map Run tetap sukses selama persentase kegagalan di bawah ambang. Inline Map terbatas concurrency-nya (hingga 40 iterasi paralel menurut dokumentasi) dan riwayat eksekusi 25.000 event, jadi tidak cocok untuk jutaan item. Loop di Lambda terkena batas 15 menit dan tidak punya pelacakan kegagalan bawaan. SQS + Lambda bisa diskalakan tetapi Anda harus membangun sendiri pengiriman key, pelacakan kegagalan, dan logika ambang 2%. Aturan umum: pemrosesan paralel massal atas objek S3 dengan toleransi kegagalan → Step Functions Distributed Map.","r":["Salah — Inline Map punya concurrency terbatas dan batas riwayat eksekusi, tidak cocok untuk jutaan item.","Salah — Loop dalam satu Lambda terkena batas waktu 15 menit dan tidak mencatat kegagalan per item secara bawaan.","Salah — Bisa diskalakan, tetapi Anda harus membuat sendiri pengisian queue, pelacakan kegagalan, dan aturan ambang 2%.","Benar — Distributed Map membaca item dari S3, berjalan sangat paralel, mencatat hasil, dan mendukung tolerated failure percentage."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'millions of S3 objects in parallel' → Step Functions Distributed Map (bukan Inline Map)."},{"id":"E2A-05","d":2,"ts":"2.1.1","t":"EMR storage and output format cost optimization","q":"A data engineering team runs nightly Apache Spark batch jobs on Amazon EMR that process about 1 PB of raw data and run for 4 hours. The output must remain available to Amazon Athena after the jobs finish. Analysts typically query only 3 of the 80 output columns and filter on a single day. The team wants to minimize both compute cost and Athena query cost. Which TWO actions should the team take? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Store input and output data in Amazon S3 and run the jobs on transient Amazon EMR clusters that terminate when the jobs finish.","Store input and output data in HDFS on a long-running Amazon EMR cluster so data stays local to the compute nodes.","Write the output to Amazon S3 as Snappy-compressed Apache Parquet files partitioned by date.","Write the output as uncompressed CSV files so that Athena does not spend time decompressing data.","Copy the output from HDFS to Amazon EBS snapshots after each run for Athena to query."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Persyaratan yang menentukan: output harus tetap tersedia untuk Athena 'after the jobs finish', analis hanya membaca '3 of the 80 output columns' dan memfilter 'a single day', serta 'minimize both compute cost and Athena query cost'. Menyimpan data di Amazon S3 (melalui EMRFS) memisahkan storage dari compute, sehingga cluster EMR bisa dibuat transient dan dimatikan setelah job selesai tanpa kehilangan data, dan Athena bisa langsung membaca S3. Athena menagih berdasarkan data yang dipindai; Parquet yang kolumnar dan terkompresi hanya membaca kolom yang diperlukan, dan partisi per tanggal membuat Athena melewati data di luar hari yang difilter (partition pruning). Distraktor terdekat adalah CSV tanpa kompresi: mudah dibaca, tetapi Athena harus memindai semua kolom dan seluruh byte teks sehingga biaya dan latensi query jauh lebih tinggi. HDFS di cluster long-running membuat cluster harus menyala terus (mahal) dan Athena tidak bisa membaca HDFS. EBS snapshot tidak dapat di-query Athena. Aturan umum: EMR hemat biaya = data di S3 + cluster transient; output untuk Athena = Parquet/ORC terkompresi + partisi sesuai filter.","r":["Benar — S3 sebagai storage persisten memungkinkan cluster transient dimatikan setelah job dan output tetap bisa di-query Athena.","Salah — Cluster long-running membayar instance sepanjang hari, dan data di HDFS hilang jika cluster dihentikan serta tidak dapat dibaca Athena.","Benar — Parquet kolumnar terkompresi dan partisi per tanggal meminimalkan data yang dipindai Athena, sehingga biaya dan latensi query turun.","Salah — CSV tanpa kompresi memaksa Athena memindai semua kolom dan seluruh byte, sehingga biaya per query jauh lebih tinggi.","Salah — Athena tidak bisa membaca EBS snapshot; langkah ini menambah biaya dan kerumitan tanpa memenuhi kebutuhan."],"k":"EMR hemat: S3 (EMRFS) + transient cluster; output untuk Athena → Parquet terkompresi + partisi sesuai filter."},{"id":"E4B-16","d":4,"ts":"4.3.3","t":"S3 replication with SSE-KMS across accounts","q":"A company replicates objects from a source S3 bucket in Account A to a destination bucket in Account B for a separate analytics team. The source objects are encrypted with SSE-KMS using a customer managed key in Account A. Account B requires that the replicas be encrypted with its own customer managed key. Which configuration meets these requirements?","o":["Enable S3 Replication with default settings; S3 automatically re-encrypts the replicas with the destination bucket's default key.","Enable replication of SSE-KMS encrypted objects in the replication rule, specify the Account B KMS key ARN as the replica encryption key, give the replication role kms:Decrypt on the source key and kms:Encrypt on the destination key, and allow the replication role in the Account B key policy.","Change the source objects to SSE-C so that replication does not need AWS KMS permissions.","Configure the destination bucket to use the AWS managed key aws/s3 and grant the replication role access to it."],"a":[1],"e":"Constraint penentu: objek sumber memakai SSE-KMS dan replika harus dienkripsi dengan 'its own customer managed key' di Account B. Secara default S3 Replication tidak mereplikasi objek SSE-KMS; Anda harus mengaktifkan replikasi objek SSE-KMS pada rule dan menentukan KMS key tujuan (replica KMS key). Replication role butuh kms:Decrypt pada kunci sumber dan kms:Encrypt pada kunci tujuan, dan karena kunci tujuan berada di akun lain, key policy Account B harus mengizinkan role tersebut. Distraktor terdekat adalah replikasi default: objek SSE-KMS justru tidak direplikasi tanpa konfigurasi tambahan. aws/s3 tidak bisa dipakai lintas akun karena key policy-nya tidak dapat diubah, dan juga bukan customer managed key. SSE-C memang dapat direplikasi, tetapi tidak memakai KMS key milik Account B dan memindahkan beban pengelolaan kunci ke pelanggan. Aturan umum: S3 Replication + SSE-KMS → aktifkan opsi replikasi SSE-KMS, tentukan replica key, atur izin KMS di kedua akun.","r":["Salah — Objek SSE-KMS tidak direplikasi secara default tanpa mengaktifkan opsi dan menentukan kunci tujuan.","Benar — Opsi replikasi SSE-KMS, replica key Account B, dan izin KMS di kedua sisi memenuhi semua syarat.","Salah — SSE-C menambah beban pengelolaan kunci dan tidak memenuhi syarat kunci KMS milik Account B.","Salah — aws/s3 bukan customer managed key dan tidak bisa dipakai principal lintas akun."],"k":"Tips ujian: S3 cross-account replication dengan SSE-KMS → enable 'replicate objects encrypted with KMS' + replica KMS key + izin key policy tujuan."},{"id":"E1A-25","d":1,"ts":"1.1.4","t":"Consuming REST APIs with Lambda","q":"A company must pull hourly weather data from a third-party REST API that returns paginated JSON and requires an API key. Each run finishes in under 2 minutes. The raw responses must be stored in Amazon S3. Which TWO actions should a data engineer take to build this solution with the LEAST operational overhead and in a secure way? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Hardcode the API key in the Lambda function's source code.","Create an Amazon EventBridge Scheduler schedule that invokes an AWS Lambda function every hour to call the API, follow the pagination, and write the raw JSON to Amazon S3.","Run a cron job on an always-on Amazon EC2 instance to call the API.","Use AWS DataSync to copy the API responses to Amazon S3.","Store the API key in AWS Secrets Manager and retrieve it from the Lambda function at runtime."],"a":[1,4],"e":"Kata kunci: REST API 'paginated JSON', 'API key', run 'under 2 minutes', dan 'LEAST operational overhead' serta 'secure'. EventBridge Scheduler yang memanggil Lambda tiap jam adalah pola serverless paling ringan untuk konsumsi API singkat; Lambda menangani pagination dan menulis respons mentah ke S3. API key sebaiknya disimpan di Secrets Manager (terenkripsi KMS, bisa dirotasi, akses via IAM), bukan di kode. Distraktor terdekat adalah cron di EC2: berfungsi, tetapi membayar instance idle dan perlu patching. Hardcode secret adalah praktik keamanan yang buruk. DataSync tidak bisa memanggil REST API. Aturan umum: konsumsi API terjadwal dan singkat = EventBridge Scheduler + Lambda, kredensial di Secrets Manager.","r":["Salah — Hardcode API key di kode adalah risiko keamanan dan menyulitkan rotasi.","Benar — Scheduler + Lambda serverless, ditagih per eksekusi, dan cukup untuk run di bawah 2 menit.","Salah — EC2 yang selalu menyala menambah biaya idle dan beban operasional.","Salah — DataSync menyalin dari sistem storage, bukan memanggil REST API.","Benar — Secrets Manager menyimpan API key secara aman dan dapat diakses Lambda melalui IAM."],"k":"Pull API terjadwal & singkat → EventBridge Scheduler + Lambda; API key → Secrets Manager."},{"id":"E1B-19","d":1,"ts":"1.2.2","t":"Glue VPC connectivity troubleshooting","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job uses a JDBC connection to read from an Amazon RDS for MySQL instance in a private subnet and writes the output to Amazon S3. The VPC has no NAT gateway or internet gateway. The job fails at startup with an error stating that the security group must allow traffic between Glue components, and after that is fixed, the job times out while writing to S3. Which TWO actions will resolve these issues? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Assign a public IP address to the RDS DB instance.","Add an inbound rule that allows port 3306 from 0.0.0.0/0 to the RDS security group.","Add a self-referencing inbound rule that allows all TCP traffic to the security group used by the Glue connection.","Create an Amazon S3 gateway VPC endpoint and associate it with the route table of the Glue connection's subnet.","Enable job bookmarks on the Glue job."],"a":[2,3],"e":"Ada dua gejala: error startup tentang komunikasi antar komponen Glue, dan timeout saat menulis ke S3 di VPC 'no NAT gateway or internet gateway'. Glue mewajibkan security group pada connection memiliki aturan inbound self-referencing untuk semua port TCP agar driver dan executor (ENI-nya) dapat saling berkomunikasi. Karena job berjalan di subnet privat tanpa NAT, akses ke S3 membutuhkan S3 gateway VPC endpoint yang dipasang pada route table subnet tersebut. Memberi IP publik ke RDS atau membuka port 3306 ke 0.0.0.0/0 tidak menyelesaikan kedua masalah dan menciptakan risiko keamanan. Job bookmark hanya mengatur pemrosesan inkremental, tidak terkait konektivitas. Aturan umum: Glue di VPC → self-referencing security group + jalur ke S3 (gateway endpoint atau NAT).","r":["Salah — IP publik tidak diperlukan karena Glue berada di VPC yang sama, dan menambah risiko keamanan.","Salah — Membuka port ke internet tidak menyelesaikan komunikasi antar komponen Glue maupun akses S3, dan tidak aman.","Benar — Aturan self-referencing all TCP diwajibkan agar komponen Glue dapat saling berkomunikasi.","Benar — Gateway endpoint S3 memberi akses privat ke S3 dari subnet tanpa NAT.","Salah — Bookmark mengatur data inkremental, bukan konektivitas jaringan."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue JDBC dalam VPC gagal → cek self-referencing SG rule (all TCP) dan S3 gateway endpoint/NAT."},{"id":"E1C-18","d":1,"ts":"1.3.2","t":"Glue job bookmarks and retries","q":"A daily AWS Glue Spark job reads new JSON files from an Amazon S3 prefix and writes Parquet output. When the job occasionally fails because of a transient network error, an operator reruns it manually, and the rerun reprocesses files from previous days. The job must automatically recover from transient failures and must process only files that have not been successfully processed before. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Enable job bookmarks for the Glue job.","Configure the job's maximum retries (number of retries) property to a value such as 2.","Switch the job to the Flex execution class.","Increase the number of workers for the job.","Run an AWS Glue crawler before every job run."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Dua kebutuhan: 'automatically recover from transient failures' dan 'process only files that have not been successfully processed'. Job bookmarks menyimpan state dari run yang sukses sehingga run berikutnya hanya membaca file baru; bookmark tidak di-commit jika run gagal, sehingga data dari run gagal diproses ulang dengan benar. Properti maximum retries membuat Glue otomatis menjalankan ulang job saat gagal tanpa campur tangan operator. Distractor terdekat adalah Flex execution class: menurunkan biaya untuk job non-mendesak, tetapi tidak menambah ketahanan dan justru bisa lebih lambat. Menambah worker tidak mencegah error jaringan atau pemrosesan ulang. Crawler memperbarui metadata, bukan melacak file yang sudah diproses. Aturan umum: pemrosesan inkremental di Glue → job bookmarks; recovery otomatis → job retries.","r":["Benar — Bookmark melacak data yang sudah diproses oleh run sukses sehingga hanya file baru yang dibaca.","Benar — Max retries menjalankan ulang job otomatis saat terjadi kegagalan sementara.","Salah — Flex adalah opsi hemat biaya untuk job tidak mendesak, bukan mekanisme fault tolerance.","Salah — Kapasitas lebih besar tidak mencegah error jaringan atau pemrosesan ulang file lama.","Salah — Crawler hanya memperbarui skema/partisi di Data Catalog."],"k":"Tips ujian: Glue 'process only new data' → job bookmarks; 'auto recover' → job retries."},{"id":"E1A-03","d":1,"ts":"1.1.1","t":"Redshift streaming ingestion","q":"An IoT analytics team ingests sensor readings into Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. Analysts need to query the data in Amazon Redshift with the LOWEST possible latency and without staging the data in Amazon S3. The team wants to avoid writing custom consumer code. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure an Amazon Data Firehose stream with the Kinesis data stream as the source and Amazon Redshift as the destination.","Run an AWS Glue streaming job that reads from the stream and writes to Amazon Redshift every 10 minutes.","Write an AWS Lambda function that reads from the stream and runs INSERT statements against Amazon Redshift through JDBC.","Use Amazon Redshift streaming ingestion by creating an external schema for the Kinesis data stream and a materialized view with auto refresh."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'LOWEST possible latency', 'without staging the data in Amazon S3', dan 'avoid writing custom consumer code'. Redshift streaming ingestion membaca langsung dari Kinesis Data Streams (atau MSK) ke dalam materialized view, tanpa staging di S3, dengan latensi hitungan detik, dan auto refresh menjaga data tetap mutakhir. Distraktor terdekat adalah Firehose ke Redshift: Firehose menulis ke bucket S3 perantara lalu menjalankan COPY, sehingga melanggar syarat 'tanpa staging S3' dan latensinya lebih tinggi karena buffering. Lambda dengan INSERT per baris adalah custom code dan tidak efisien untuk Redshift (columnar, lebih cocok untuk bulk load). Aturan umum: KDS/MSK → Redshift dengan latensi rendah tanpa S3 = Redshift streaming ingestion (materialized view).","r":["Salah — Firehose ke Redshift men-stage data di S3 lalu menjalankan COPY, sehingga melanggar syarat tanpa staging dan latensinya lebih tinggi.","Salah — Interval 10 menit tidak memenuhi 'lowest latency', dan tetap memerlukan kode Glue job.","Salah — Ini custom code, dan INSERT baris per baris lewat JDBC tidak efisien untuk Redshift.","Benar — Redshift streaming ingestion membaca KDS langsung ke materialized view dengan latensi rendah, tanpa S3 dan tanpa kode consumer."],"k":"KDS/MSK → Redshift, latensi terendah, tanpa S3 → Redshift streaming ingestion + materialized view."},{"id":"E2C-04","d":2,"ts":"2.4.1","t":"DynamoDB partition key and sort key design","q":"A company is designing an Amazon DynamoDB table for an order management service. The main access pattern is to retrieve all orders for a given customer, sorted by order date, and to retrieve only the orders placed within a specific date range for that customer. Each customer can have thousands of orders. Which key design meets these requirements MOST efficiently?","o":["Use order_id as the partition key and create a Scan with a filter expression on customer_id and order_date.","Use customer_id as the partition key and a composite sort key such as order_date#order_id.","Use order_date as the partition key and customer_id as the sort key.","Use a random UUID as the partition key and store customer_id and order_date as non-key attributes."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah 'retrieve all orders for a given customer, sorted by order date' dan 'within a specific date range'. Di DynamoDB, desain key harus dimulai dari access pattern: partition key customer_id mengelompokkan semua order satu customer, dan sort key yang diawali order_date membuat item tersimpan terurut sehingga Query dengan kondisi BETWEEN atau begins_with bisa mengambil range tanggal secara efisien. Menambahkan order_id di sort key (order_date#order_id) menjamin keunikan jika ada beberapa order di tanggal yang sama. Scan dengan filter membaca seluruh tabel dan mahal dalam RCU. Partition key order_date menyebabkan hot partition pada tanggal hari ini dan tidak mendukung query per customer. UUID acak menyebar beban dengan baik tetapi tidak mendukung access pattern apa pun selain lookup langsung. Aturan umum: partition key = entitas yang di-query, sort key = atribut untuk sorting/range.","r":["Salah — Scan membaca seluruh tabel lalu memfilter, sehingga lambat dan boros kapasitas baca.","Benar — Partition key customer_id plus sort key order_date#order_id mendukung Query terurut dan range tanggal per customer.","Salah — order_date sebagai partition key menimbulkan hot partition dan tidak bisa mengambil semua order satu customer dengan satu Query.","Salah — UUID acak tidak mendukung Query per customer atau range tanggal tanpa Scan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'get items for X sorted/range by Y' di DynamoDB → partition key X, sort key Y (composite jika perlu unik)."},{"id":"E1A-49","d":1,"ts":"1.1.8","t":"NAT gateway Elastic IP allowlisting","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job runs in private subnets of a VPC and must call a third-party data provider's HTTPS API. The provider only accepts connections from IP addresses on its allowlist and needs a single, stable IP address from the company. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Give the provider the private IP addresses of the Glue job's elastic network interfaces.","Route the subnets' internet-bound traffic through a NAT gateway with an Elastic IP address, and give the provider that Elastic IP address to allowlist.","Give the provider the published IP ranges for AWS Glue in the Region.","Create a VPC gateway endpoint for the provider's API."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: job di 'private subnets', provider memakai 'allowlist' dan meminta 'single, stable IP address'. Resource di subnet privat keluar ke internet melalui NAT gateway, dan NAT gateway memakai Elastic IP yang statis, sehingga semua trafik keluar dari Glue tampil dengan satu IP publik tetap yang bisa di-allowlist oleh provider. Distraktor terdekat adalah memberikan IP privat ENI: IP privat tidak terlihat di internet dan bisa berubah setiap run. Rentang IP Glue untuk Region sangat luas dan dipakai bersama pelanggan lain, sehingga tidak aman untuk allowlist. Gateway endpoint hanya tersedia untuk S3 dan DynamoDB. Aturan umum: workload di VPC (Glue, Lambda, EMR) ke API eksternal yang memakai IP allowlist = NAT gateway + Elastic IP.","r":["Salah — IP privat tidak dapat dirutekan di internet dan dapat berubah setiap run.","Benar — NAT gateway dengan Elastic IP memberi satu IP publik tetap untuk semua trafik keluar.","Salah — Rentang IP layanan sangat luas dan dipakai bersama, sehingga allowlist menjadi tidak bermakna.","Salah — Gateway endpoint hanya untuk Amazon S3 dan DynamoDB, bukan API pihak ketiga."],"k":"Workload di VPC → API pihak ketiga dengan IP allowlist → NAT gateway + Elastic IP."},{"id":"E2B-03","d":2,"ts":"2.2.2","t":"Glue Data Catalog as Hive metastore for EMR","q":"A company runs transient Amazon EMR clusters for nightly Apache Spark jobs. Data analysts also query the same Amazon S3 datasets with Amazon Athena. Currently each EMR cluster stores table definitions in a local Hive metastore, so the definitions are lost when the cluster terminates and do not match the tables in Athena. The company wants one persistent metastore shared by EMR and Athena with the LEAST operational overhead. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Configure the EMR clusters to use the AWS Glue Data Catalog as the Apache Hive metastore through the spark-hive-site and hive-site configuration classifications.","Create an Amazon RDS for MySQL database as an external Hive metastore for the EMR clusters and export the DDL to Athena every night.","Keep the local Hive metastore and back up the metastore database to Amazon S3 before each cluster terminates.","Store the table schemas as JSON documents in an Amazon DynamoDB table and read them at the start of every Spark job."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya: 'transient EMR clusters', 'one persistent metastore shared by EMR and Athena' dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. AWS Glue Data Catalog kompatibel dengan Apache Hive metastore, bersifat serverless dan persisten di luar umur cluster, dan merupakan catalog bawaan yang dipakai Athena. Dengan mengaktifkan setting 'Use for Hive/Spark table metadata' (classification hive-site/spark-hive-site), EMR dan Athena melihat definisi tabel yang sama. External metastore di RDS MySQL memang membuat metadata persisten untuk EMR, tetapi Anda harus mengelola database dan Athena tetap tidak membacanya secara native, sehingga perlu sinkronisasi DDL. Backup metastore lokal dan katalog buatan sendiri di DynamoDB jelas menambah pekerjaan. Aturan umum: metastore bersama untuk EMR, Athena, Glue dan Redshift Spectrum → Glue Data Catalog.","r":["Benar — Glue Data Catalog menjadi Hive metastore yang persisten dan sama untuk EMR dan Athena, tanpa server yang perlu dikelola.","Salah — RDS sebagai Hive metastore butuh pengelolaan database dan sinkronisasi DDL manual ke Athena.","Salah — Backup/restore metastore lokal rawan gagal dan tetap tidak membagi metadata ke Athena.","Salah — Katalog buatan sendiri di DynamoDB tidak dikenali Spark SQL maupun Athena dan menambah kode kustom."],"k":"Tips ujian: EMR + 'persistent/shared metastore' + Athena → pakai Glue Data Catalog sebagai Hive metastore."},{"id":"E2B-14","d":2,"ts":"2.2.1","t":"Athena Federated Query","q":"A marketing team stores campaign events in Amazon S3, cataloged in the AWS Glue Data Catalog. Customer master data lives in an Amazon RDS for MySQL database that is updated continuously. Analysts need to join both datasets with SQL in Amazon Athena by using the current customer data, and the company does not want to build a pipeline that copies the customer table. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use Amazon Athena Federated Query with the MySQL data source connector, register the connector as a data catalog in Athena, and join it with the Data Catalog tables.","Use AWS DMS to replicate the customer table to Amazon S3 every hour and crawl the output.","Create an Amazon Redshift Spectrum external schema for the RDS for MySQL database.","Create an AWS Glue crawler that crawls the MySQL database so that Athena can query it as a Data Catalog table."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: 'current customer data', 'join both datasets with SQL in Amazon Athena' dan 'does not want to build a pipeline that copies'. Athena Federated Query memakai data source connector (fungsi Lambda) yang didaftarkan sebagai data catalog tambahan di Athena, sehingga satu query bisa menggabungkan tabel Glue Data Catalog di S3 dengan tabel MySQL langsung dari sumbernya. Data pelanggan selalu terbaru karena dibaca saat query berjalan. DMS ke S3 adalah pipeline penyalinan dan datanya bisa tertinggal hingga satu jam. Crawler JDBC hanya membuat definisi tabel; Athena tidak bisa membaca tabel JDBC dari Data Catalog tanpa connector. Redshift Spectrum untuk data S3, bukan RDS. Ingat: Athena + sumber non-S3 + tanpa copy → Athena Federated Query.","r":["Benar — Federated Query membaca MySQL langsung saat query dan menggabungkannya dengan tabel S3 di Data Catalog.","Salah — Replikasi DMS adalah pipeline penyalinan yang dilarang dan datanya tidak real time.","Salah — Spectrum membaca data S3 lewat external schema, bukan database RDS MySQL.","Salah — Crawler JDBC hanya membuat metadata; Athena tidak memakainya untuk membaca data RDS secara langsung."],"k":"Tips ujian: Athena join S3 dengan RDS/DynamoDB 'tanpa copy' → Athena Federated Query (Lambda connector)."},{"id":"E3A-16","d":3,"ts":"3.1.4","t":"Amazon Redshift MERGE and stored procedures","q":"A data engineer loads daily change files from Amazon S3 into Amazon Redshift. Each file contains new and updated customer records. The target table must be updated so that existing customers are modified and new customers are inserted. The process should run entirely inside Amazon Redshift every night with the LEAST additional infrastructure. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use COPY to load the file into a staging table, then run a MERGE statement into the target table inside a stored procedure that is run by the Amazon Redshift query scheduler.","Use an AWS Lambda function that reads each record from S3 and runs an individual INSERT or UPDATE statement through JDBC.","Use COPY directly into the target table and rely on the primary key constraint to reject duplicates.","Export the target table to S3 with UNLOAD, merge the data with an Amazon EMR cluster, and reload the full table."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'modified and inserted' (upsert), 'entirely inside Amazon Redshift', dan 'LEAST additional infrastructure'. Pola standar di Redshift adalah COPY ke staging table (cepat dan paralel), lalu MERGE ke target untuk update baris yang cocok dan insert baris baru. Membungkusnya dalam stored procedure dan menjadwalkannya dengan query scheduler Redshift (yang berbasis EventBridge) menjaga semua logika di dalam Redshift. Constraint primary key di Redshift bersifat informasional dan tidak ditegakkan, jadi COPY langsung akan menghasilkan duplikat. INSERT/UPDATE per baris lewat Lambda sangat lambat untuk data warehouse kolumnar. UNLOAD + EMR + reload penuh adalah infrastruktur berlebihan. Aturan umum: upsert di Redshift → COPY ke staging + MERGE.","r":["Benar — COPY ke staging + MERGE di stored procedure yang dijadwalkan adalah upsert efisien di dalam Redshift.","Salah — Operasi per baris lewat JDBC sangat lambat di Redshift dan menambah komponen Lambda.","Salah — Primary key di Redshift tidak ditegakkan, sehingga duplikat tetap masuk.","Salah — Menambah EMR dan reload penuh adalah overhead besar yang tidak perlu."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift upsert → COPY ke staging table lalu MERGE; primary key Redshift tidak ditegakkan."},{"id":"E4A-39","d":4,"ts":"4.2.3","t":"Redshift default privileges","q":"In an Amazon Redshift data warehouse, an ETL user named etl_loader creates new tables in the sales schema every day. Members of the analysts group must be able to read all existing tables in the schema and every table that etl_loader creates in the future, without manual grants after each load. Which set of SQL statements meets this requirement?","o":["GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA sales TO GROUP analysts; and nothing else.","GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA sales TO GROUP analysts;","GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA sales TO GROUP analysts; GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA sales TO GROUP analysts; ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR USER etl_loader IN SCHEMA sales GRANT SELECT ON TABLES TO GROUP analysts;","ALTER USER etl_loader CREATEUSER; and let analysts query the tables as etl_loader."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci: 'all existing tables' dan 'every table that etl_loader creates in the future'. Di Amazon Redshift, GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA hanya berlaku untuk tabel yang ada saat perintah dijalankan. Untuk tabel masa depan, gunakan ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES FOR USER (pembuat tabel) IN SCHEMA, yang otomatis memberi hak pada objek baru yang dibuat user tersebut. Grup juga butuh USAGE pada schema agar dapat mengakses objek di dalamnya. GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA hanya memberi hak level schema (CREATE dan USAGE), bukan SELECT pada tabel. Memberi CREATEUSER kepada etl_loader dan berbagi user melanggar least privilege dan akuntabilitas. Aturan umum: tabel lama = GRANT ... ON ALL TABLES; tabel baru = ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES.","r":["Salah — Hanya mencakup tabel yang sudah ada, dan tanpa USAGE pada schema analis tetap tidak bisa mengakses.","Salah — Hak schema tidak memberi SELECT pada tabel di dalamnya.","Benar — USAGE, SELECT pada tabel yang ada, dan default privileges untuk tabel masa depan memenuhi semua kebutuhan.","Salah — Berbagi user ETL dan memberi CREATEUSER melanggar least privilege dan tidak dapat diaudit."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'future tables' di Redshift → ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES; jangan lupa GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA."},{"id":"E1C-65","d":1,"ts":"1.4.5","t":"CloudFormation drift detection","q":"An AWS Glue job and its Amazon S3 buckets are deployed with AWS CloudFormation. An auditor suspects that someone changed the job's worker type and number of workers directly in the AWS Glue console, which is against policy. The data engineer must identify which resource properties differ from the template with the LEAST effort. What should the engineer do?","o":["Run drift detection on the CloudFormation stack and review the drift details for the Glue job resource.","Delete and recreate the stack to restore the original configuration.","Search AWS CloudTrail logs manually and compare each API call with the template.","Create a new change set with the same template and look for differences."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhannya mengidentifikasi 'which resource properties differ from the template' akibat perubahan manual, dengan 'LEAST effort'. CloudFormation drift detection membandingkan konfigurasi aktual resource dengan konfigurasi yang diharapkan dari template, lalu menampilkan status DRIFTED dan detail properti yang berbeda (nilai yang diharapkan vs nilai aktual). Distractor terdekat adalah CloudTrail: dapat menunjukkan siapa yang mengubah, tetapi membandingkan setiap panggilan API dengan template secara manual memerlukan banyak usaha. Change set dengan template yang sama membandingkan template dengan template sebelumnya, bukan dengan kondisi aktual resource. Menghapus stack bersifat merusak dan tidak mengidentifikasi perbedaan. Aturan umum: perubahan manual di luar IaC → CloudFormation drift detection.","r":["Benar — Drift detection langsung menunjukkan properti yang berbeda antara template dan resource aktual.","Salah — Merusak dan tidak memberi informasi tentang perbedaan.","Salah — Bisa membantu audit, tetapi perbandingan manual memerlukan banyak usaha.","Salah — Change set membandingkan template, bukan kondisi aktual resource."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'someone changed resources outside CloudFormation' → drift detection."},{"id":"E1B-14","d":1,"ts":"1.2.1","t":"EKS node autoscaling for data workloads","q":"A company runs Apache Spark jobs on Amazon EKS. The cluster uses managed node groups with a single fixed instance type. During peak runs, many executor pods remain in Pending state for several minutes, and during off-peak hours nodes are underutilized. The company wants faster, right-sized node provisioning and lower cost, including use of Spot capacity where possible. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Set the minimum size of each node group equal to its maximum size so capacity is always available.","Increase the executor memory settings in the Spark configuration so fewer executors are requested.","Deploy Karpenter to provision just-in-time nodes from a flexible set of instance types, including Spot Instances, and to consolidate underutilized nodes.","Manually create an additional larger node group before each peak run and delete it afterward."],"a":[2],"e":"Masalahnya adalah pod 'Pending' saat puncak (scaling lambat) dan node 'underutilized' di luar puncak, dengan tujuan 'faster, right-sized node provisioning' serta Spot. Karpenter adalah node autoscaler untuk Kubernetes yang langsung memprovisi node sesuai kebutuhan pod yang pending, memilih dari banyak instance type (termasuk Spot), dan melakukan konsolidasi node yang kurang terpakai untuk menekan biaya. Menyetel minimum sama dengan maksimum menghilangkan Pending, tetapi membayar kapasitas puncak 24 jam sehingga melanggar tujuan biaya. Menaikkan memori executor tidak mengatasi kekurangan node dan bisa memperburuk bin-packing. Membuat node group manual setiap kali menambah beban operasional. Aturan umum: optimasi container di EKS untuk beban bervariasi → autoscaling node yang fleksibel (Karpenter) dengan Spot dan konsolidasi.","r":["Salah — Kapasitas selalu tersedia, tetapi biaya sangat tinggi karena node puncak berjalan terus.","Salah — Mengubah ukuran executor tidak menambah kapasitas node dan tidak mengatasi underutilization.","Benar — Karpenter memprovisi node tepat waktu dan berukuran sesuai, mendukung Spot, dan mengonsolidasikan node yang kurang terpakai.","Salah — Proses manual menambah overhead operasional dan rawan kesalahan."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'EKS pods Pending + underutilized nodes + Spot' → Karpenter (just-in-time, right-sized nodes, consolidation)."},{"id":"E2A-38","d":2,"ts":"2.1.4","t":"AWS DMS CDC to S3","q":"A company runs an on-premises MySQL database that supports a 24/7 order application. The analytics team wants the order tables replicated to an Amazon S3 data lake in Parquet format, including all ongoing inserts, updates, and deletes, with only a few minutes of delay. The source database must not be taken offline. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use mysqldump every night and upload the files to Amazon S3 with the AWS CLI.","Use AWS DataSync to copy the MySQL data directory to Amazon S3 every hour.","Use AWS DMS with a full load plus change data capture (CDC) task and an Amazon S3 target endpoint configured for Parquet output.","Use AWS Transfer Family to receive exported CSV files from the database server."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci adalah 'including all ongoing inserts, updates, and deletes', 'a few minutes of delay', dan sumber 'must not be taken offline'. AWS DMS dengan tipe migrasi full load + CDC pertama menyalin data yang ada, lalu membaca binary log MySQL untuk mereplikasi perubahan berkelanjutan tanpa downtime; target S3 dapat menulis file Parquet beserta kolom operasi (I/U/D) untuk diproses di data lake. Distraktor terdekat adalah mysqldump harian: tidak memerlukan downtime, tetapi keterlambatan satu hari dan tidak menangkap perubahan secara bertahap. DataSync menyalin file, bukan transaksi; menyalin data directory database yang sedang aktif menghasilkan file yang tidak konsisten. Transfer Family hanya penerima file dan tetap membutuhkan proses ekspor terpisah. Aturan umum: replikasi database berkelanjutan dengan downtime minimal → DMS full load + CDC.","r":["Salah — Dump harian tidak memenuhi keterlambatan beberapa menit dan tidak menangkap perubahan secara inkremental.","Salah — DataSync menyalin file mentah dari database aktif sehingga hasilnya tidak konsisten dan tidak menangkap perubahan transaksional.","Benar — DMS full load + CDC mereplikasi data awal dan perubahan berkelanjutan ke S3 dalam Parquet tanpa menghentikan sumber.","Salah — Transfer Family hanya menerima file; ekspor CSV tetap harus dibangun dan tidak memberikan CDC."],"k":"Ongoing changes from a live DB with minimal downtime → AWS DMS full load + CDC."},{"id":"E1C-38","d":1,"ts":"1.3.4","t":"SQS FIFO message groups","q":"A pipeline emits status messages (STARTED, LOADED, VALIDATED, PUBLISHED) for each of hundreds of datasets. A downstream service must process the messages for each dataset in the exact order they were sent and must not process the same message twice, but messages for different datasets can be processed in parallel. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Use an Amazon SQS standard queue with long polling enabled.","Use an Amazon SQS FIFO queue, set the MessageGroupId to the dataset ID, and use content-based deduplication or a MessageDeduplicationId.","Use an Amazon SQS FIFO queue with the same MessageGroupId for all messages.","Use an Amazon SNS standard topic with an AWS Lambda subscriber."],"a":[1],"e":"Kebutuhannya: urutan 'exact order' per dataset, 'not process the same message twice', namun dataset berbeda 'can be processed in parallel'. SQS FIFO menjamin urutan dalam satu message group dan deduplikasi dalam jendela 5 menit; dengan MessageGroupId = dataset ID, setiap dataset berurutan sementara grup yang berbeda bisa diproses paralel. Distractor terdekat adalah FIFO dengan satu MessageGroupId untuk semua pesan: urutan dan dedup terjaga, tetapi semua pesan diproses satu per satu, sehingga paralelisme antar dataset hilang. SQS standard dan SNS standard hanya best-effort ordering dan at-least-once. Aturan umum: urutan per entitas + paralel antar entitas → SQS FIFO dengan MessageGroupId per entitas.","r":["Salah — Antrean standard tidak menjamin urutan dan bisa mengirim pesan lebih dari sekali.","Benar — Message group per dataset menjaga urutan per dataset, dedup mencegah duplikat, dan grup berbeda berjalan paralel.","Salah — Satu message group memaksa semua pesan diproses berurutan sehingga paralelisme hilang.","Salah — SNS standard tidak menjamin urutan atau pengiriman tepat sekali."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'ordered per key + parallel across keys' → SQS FIFO, MessageGroupId = key."},{"id":"E1B-38","d":1,"ts":"1.2.4","t":"Glue partition pruning with pushdown predicates","q":"An AWS Glue ETL job reads a Glue Data Catalog table that contains 5 years of clickstream data in Amazon S3, partitioned by year, month, and day. The job needs only the last 2 days of data, but it currently loads the whole table and then filters it, which makes each run slow and expensive. Which change will reduce cost the MOST?","o":["Pass a push_down_predicate on the partition columns when creating the DynamicFrame so that only the required partitions are read.","Apply a Filter transform on the date column after the DynamicFrame is created.","Increase the number of workers so that the full table is read faster.","Run an AWS Glue crawler before each job run."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kuncinya adalah tabel 'partitioned by year, month, and day' sementara job 'loads the whole table and then filters it'. Dengan push_down_predicate pada kolom partisi saat membuat DynamicFrame dari Data Catalog, Glue hanya membaca partisi yang cocok (2 hari) sehingga data yang dipindai, waktu run, dan DPU-hour turun drastis. Filter transform adalah distraktor terdekat karena hasil akhirnya sama, tetapi filter dijalankan setelah seluruh data dibaca sehingga biaya tidak berkurang. Menambah worker hanya mempercepat pembacaan seluruh tabel dengan biaya lebih tinggi. Crawler hanya memperbarui metadata dan tidak mengurangi data yang dibaca. Aturan umum: baca sebagian partisi di Glue → push_down_predicate (partition pruning) sebelum data dimuat.","r":["Benar — Predicate pushdown memangkas partisi yang dibaca sehingga biaya dan waktu turun.","Salah — Filter setelah load tetap membaca seluruh 5 tahun data.","Salah — Lebih banyak worker berarti biaya lebih tinggi untuk membaca data yang tidak diperlukan.","Salah — Crawler memperbarui metadata, tidak membatasi data yang dibaca job."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'Glue reads all partitions then filters' → push_down_predicate pada kolom partisi."},{"id":"E3B-15","d":3,"ts":"3.3.2","t":"Amazon Managed Grafana","q":"A data operations team wants a single set of operational dashboards that combine Amazon CloudWatch metrics from AWS Glue and Amazon EMR, pipeline status rows stored in Amazon Redshift, and results of Amazon Athena queries, without copying the data into another store. The team does not want to manage servers, patching, or plugin upgrades. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Install open source Grafana on an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer.","Create an Amazon Managed Grafana workspace with dashboards that use the CloudWatch, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon Athena data sources.","Build CloudWatch dashboards and publish the Redshift table rows as custom metrics by using a scheduled Lambda function.","Use OpenSearch Dashboards after ingesting all metrics and Redshift tables into an Amazon OpenSearch Service domain."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kuncinya: menggabungkan beberapa sumber (CloudWatch, Redshift, Athena) 'without copying the data', dan 'does not want to manage servers, patching, or plugin upgrades'. Amazon Managed Grafana adalah layanan Grafana terkelola yang mendukung data source seperti CloudWatch, Redshift, Athena, OpenSearch, dan Prometheus, yang meng-query data langsung dari sumbernya, dan AWS yang mengelola infrastruktur serta upgrade-nya. Distraktor terdekat adalah Grafana open source di EC2 — fungsional tetapi melanggar syarat tanpa server dan patching. CloudWatch dashboards membutuhkan Lambda kustom untuk menyalin tabel Redshift menjadi metrik. OpenSearch membutuhkan ingestion (penyalinan) semua data. Aturan: dashboard operasional multi-source tanpa infrastruktur → Amazon Managed Grafana.","r":["Salah — Grafana self-managed membutuhkan pengelolaan server, patching, dan upgrade plugin.","Benar — Managed Grafana menyediakan data source CloudWatch, Redshift, dan Athena yang meng-query data di tempatnya, tanpa server yang harus dikelola.","Salah — Butuh kode kustom untuk menyalin data Redshift sebagai metrik, menambah overhead.","Salah — Harus menyalin semua metrik dan tabel ke OpenSearch, menambah pipeline dan biaya."],"k":"Tips ujian: dashboard operasional dari banyak data source AWS tanpa server → Amazon Managed Grafana."},{"id":"E3A-50","d":3,"ts":"3.2.2","t":"Data validation with Lambda","q":"Partners upload JSON files to an Amazon S3 landing prefix throughout the day. Each file must be checked immediately for required fields and valid date formats. Valid files must be moved to a processing prefix, and invalid files must be moved to a quarantine prefix with an error report so that bad data never reaches downstream jobs. The files are small. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Run an AWS Glue crawler on the landing prefix every hour and drop tables with schema changes.","Load all files into Amazon Redshift and delete invalid rows each night.","Trigger an AWS Lambda function from S3 object-created events that validates each file and copies it to the processing or quarantine prefix, writing an error report for invalid files.","Ask partners to validate files before uploading them."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'checked immediately', 'valid to processing, invalid to quarantine', 'bad data never reaches downstream', dan 'small files'. Lambda yang dipicu event S3 berjalan segera saat setiap file tiba, memvalidasi field wajib dan format tanggal, lalu menyalin file ke prefix processing atau quarantine beserta laporan error. Ini pola 'quarantine' yang umum, serverless, dan murah untuk file kecil. Crawler hanya mendeteksi skema di katalog, tidak memvalidasi nilai per record, dan berjalan per jam. Memuat ke Redshift dulu berarti data buruk sudah masuk ke sistem downstream. Mengandalkan partner tidak bisa dijamin. Aturan umum: validasi per file saat tiba → S3 event + Lambda dengan prefix quarantine.","r":["Salah — Crawler tidak memvalidasi nilai per record dan tidak berjalan seketika.","Salah — Data buruk sudah masuk ke warehouse sebelum dibersihkan.","Benar — Lambda berbasis event memvalidasi setiap file seketika dan memisahkan file valid dan tidak valid.","Salah — Tidak ada jaminan atau kontrol atas validasi di sisi partner."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'validate each file on arrival + quarantine bad data' → S3 event + Lambda."},{"id":"E3B-62","d":3,"ts":"3.4.4","t":"Reservoir sampling","q":"A streaming application processes an unbounded stream of sensor readings whose total size is unknown. A data engineer needs to maintain a uniform random sample of exactly 10,000 readings at any point in time, using a single pass over the data and fixed memory. Which sampling technique meets these requirements?","o":["Systematic sampling that keeps every 1,000th reading.","Stratified sampling by sensor type.","Reservoir sampling.","Taking the first 10,000 readings and ignoring the rest."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'unbounded stream', 'total size is unknown', 'exactly 10,000 readings', 'single pass', dan 'fixed memory'. Reservoir sampling menyimpan reservoir berukuran k; setiap item baru ke-n menggantikan item acak di reservoir dengan probabilitas k/n, sehingga setiap item yang pernah lewat memiliki peluang yang sama untuk berada di sampel, hanya dengan satu kali lintasan dan memori tetap. Distraktor terdekat adalah systematic sampling setiap item ke-1.000: ukuran sampel terus bertambah karena total data tidak diketahui, dan bisa bias jika data periodik. Stratified sampling butuh pengetahuan strata dan tidak menjamin ukuran tetap. Mengambil 10.000 pertama sangat bias. Aturan: sampel seragam berukuran tetap dari stream tak terbatas → reservoir sampling.","r":["Salah — Ukuran sampel bertambah terus seiring stream dan rentan bias terhadap pola periodik.","Salah — Stratifikasi tidak menjamin ukuran tetap dan butuh informasi strata di awal.","Benar — Reservoir sampling menjaga sampel acak seragam berukuran tetap dalam satu lintasan.","Salah — Hanya merepresentasikan awal stream dan sangat bias."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'unknown/unbounded stream + fixed-size uniform sample' → reservoir sampling."},{"id":"E1C-73","d":1,"ts":"1.4.9","t":"CodeBuild buildspec","q":"A team is adding an AWS CodeBuild stage to its data pipeline's CI/CD process. The stage must install Python dependencies, run pytest and a linter on the AWS Glue scripts, and produce a packaged artifact for later deployment stages. The build steps must be version-controlled together with the code. Where should the data engineer define these steps?","o":["In a buildspec.yml file in the source repository that defines install, pre_build, build, and post_build phases and the output artifacts.","In the AWS CodePipeline manual approval action configuration.","In the AWS CloudFormation template's Outputs section.","In an appspec.yml file used by AWS CodeDeploy."],"a":[0],"e":"Kebutuhannya: perintah build (install dependensi, pytest, linter, packaging) untuk CodeBuild yang 'version-controlled together with the code'. CodeBuild membaca file buildspec.yml (biasanya di root repositori) yang mendefinisikan fase install, pre_build, build, post_build, serta bagian artifacts dan reports untuk hasil tes. Karena berada di repositori, perubahan langkah build ikut di-review dan diversikan bersama kode. Distractor terdekat adalah appspec.yml: ini file untuk CodeDeploy yang mengatur langkah deployment dan hooks, bukan langkah build dan tes. Manual approval action hanya gerbang persetujuan. Bagian Outputs CloudFormation hanya mengekspor nilai stack. Aturan umum: CodeBuild → buildspec.yml; CodeDeploy → appspec.yml.","r":["Benar — buildspec.yml mendefinisikan fase build dan artefak CodeBuild serta disimpan di repositori.","Salah — Approval action tidak menjalankan perintah build atau tes.","Salah — Outputs mengekspor nilai stack, bukan langkah build.","Salah — appspec.yml untuk deployment CodeDeploy, bukan langkah build dan tes."],"k":"Tips ujian: CodeBuild commands → buildspec.yml; CodeDeploy → appspec.yml."},{"id":"E1A-26","d":1,"ts":"1.1.4","t":"AWS Data Exchange auto-export","q":"A company subscribes to a third-party financial dataset through AWS Data Exchange. The provider publishes a new revision every business day. The company wants each new revision to be delivered to its Amazon S3 data lake automatically, without writing custom code. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Configure an auto-export job for the AWS Data Exchange data set to export new revisions to the Amazon S3 bucket.","Write an AWS Lambda function that polls the provider's website and downloads new files.","Ask the provider to upload files through an AWS Transfer Family SFTP server.","Create an AWS Glue crawler that points at the AWS Data Exchange data set."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci: dataset dari 'AWS Data Exchange', 'new revision every business day', dan 'without writing custom code'. AWS Data Exchange mendukung auto-export: setiap kali provider menerbitkan revision baru, aset otomatis diekspor ke bucket S3 yang ditentukan. Ini menghilangkan kebutuhan polling dan kode. Distraktor terdekat adalah Lambda yang melakukan polling: berfungsi, tetapi berupa kode kustom dan tidak memakai mekanisme langganan yang sudah ada. Meminta provider memakai SFTP mengabaikan kanal Data Exchange yang sudah dibayar. Glue crawler hanya membaca metadata dari lokasi data (misalnya S3), tidak bisa menarik aset dari Data Exchange. Aturan umum: data pihak ketiga via Data Exchange ke S3 otomatis = auto-export revisions.","r":["Benar — Auto-export mengirim setiap revision baru ke S3 secara otomatis tanpa kode.","Salah — Polling dengan Lambda adalah kode kustom dan tidak memanfaatkan langganan Data Exchange.","Salah — Mengabaikan mekanisme Data Exchange dan membutuhkan perubahan dari sisi provider.","Salah — Crawler tidak bisa menarik aset dari Data Exchange; ia hanya membuat metadata."],"k":"Langganan AWS Data Exchange → S3 otomatis → auto-export job untuk revision baru."},{"id":"E3A-48","d":3,"ts":"3.2.2","t":"Deduplication with window functions","q":"An Amazon Athena table of customer profiles contains multiple versions of the same customer_id because updates are appended with an updated_at timestamp. Analysts need a clean table that keeps only the latest version of each customer, stored as Parquet in Amazon S3, without using any other service. Which TWO steps should the data engineer combine? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Use SELECT DISTINCT * to remove the older versions.","Use ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY updated_at DESC) and keep only rows where the row number equals 1.","Use GROUP BY customer_id with MAX(updated_at) and select all other columns without aggregation.","Write the result with a CREATE TABLE AS SELECT (CTAS) statement using format = 'PARQUET'.","Run MSCK REPAIR TABLE on the source table to merge the duplicate rows."],"a":[1,3],"e":"Kata kuncinya 'keep only the latest version', 'stored as Parquet', dan 'without any other service'. Fungsi window ROW_NUMBER() dengan PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY updated_at DESC memberi nomor 1 pada versi terbaru setiap customer, lalu filter row number = 1 menyisakan satu baris per customer. CTAS dengan format Parquet menulis hasil bersih ke S3 sekaligus membuat tabel baru di Glue Data Catalog, semuanya di Athena. SELECT DISTINCT hanya menghapus baris yang identik di semua kolom, sedangkan versi lama dan baru memiliki nilai berbeda. GROUP BY dengan kolom non-agregat tidak valid secara SQL. MSCK REPAIR TABLE hanya menambahkan partisi ke katalog, tidak mengubah data. Aturan umum: deduplikasi 'latest record per key' → ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY key ORDER BY ts DESC) = 1.","r":["Salah — DISTINCT hanya menghapus baris yang identik sepenuhnya, bukan versi lama dengan nilai berbeda.","Benar — ROW_NUMBER per customer_id yang diurutkan dari terbaru memilih tepat satu baris terbaru.","Salah — Memilih kolom non-agregat tanpa GROUP BY adalah SQL yang tidak valid.","Benar — CTAS menulis hasil bersih sebagai Parquet di S3 dan mendaftarkan tabel baru.","Salah — MSCK REPAIR TABLE hanya memuat metadata partisi dan tidak menghapus duplikat."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'keep latest record per key' → ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY ... ORDER BY ts DESC) = 1, lalu CTAS."},{"id":"E4B-51","d":4,"ts":"4.5.4","t":"Config timeline with CloudTrail correlation","q":"A security engineer notices that the security group attached to an Amazon Redshift cluster now allows inbound traffic on port 5439 from 0.0.0.0/0. The engineer must determine what the previous rules were, when the change occurred, and which IAM principal made the change, by using a single console view where possible. Which solution meets these requirements?","o":["Analyze VPC Flow Logs for the cluster's network interfaces.","Review the Amazon CloudWatch metrics of the Redshift cluster.","Review Amazon GuardDuty findings for the account.","Open the AWS Config resource timeline for the security group, compare the configuration items before and after the change, and view the linked CloudTrail event that shows the principal."],"a":[3],"e":"Kata kunci: 'what the previous rules were', 'when the change occurred', dan 'which IAM principal', idealnya dari 'a single console view'. Resource timeline AWS Config menampilkan configuration item security group sebelum dan sesudah perubahan beserta waktunya, dan untuk perubahan yang tercatat menampilkan event CloudTrail terkait (misalnya AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress) yang berisi identitas pemanggil. Dengan demikian ketiga pertanyaan terjawab dari satu tampilan. Distraktor terdekat adalah VPC Flow Logs: menunjukkan trafik jaringan yang diterima/ditolak, bukan konfigurasi atau siapa yang mengubahnya. CloudWatch metrics Redshift berisi performa cluster. GuardDuty mungkin mendeteksi aktivitas mencurigakan, tetapi tidak memberikan diff konfigurasi sebelumnya. Aturan umum: perubahan konfigurasi + siapa pelakunya → Config timeline (dengan tautan ke CloudTrail).","r":["Salah — Flow Logs mencatat trafik jaringan, bukan perubahan aturan atau pelakunya.","Salah — Metrics Redshift berisi data performa, bukan konfigurasi security group.","Salah — GuardDuty mendeteksi ancaman, tidak menampilkan konfigurasi sebelumnya.","Benar — Config timeline menampilkan konfigurasi sebelum/sesudah, waktu perubahan, dan event CloudTrail terkait."],"k":"Tips ujian: Config timeline = before/after config + link ke CloudTrail event (who)."},{"id":"E4B-45","d":4,"ts":"4.5.2","t":"Custom PII identifiers","q":"A company uses a proprietary employee identifier with the format EMP- followed by 6 digits (for example, EMP-482913). The identifier is considered sensitive. The company must detect it in objects stored in Amazon S3 and also in records processed by AWS Glue ETL jobs before they reach the curated zone. Which TWO actions meet these requirements? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Rely on the Amazon Macie managed data identifiers to detect the employee identifier.","Create an Amazon Macie custom data identifier that uses a regular expression for the EMP- pattern and include it in the sensitive data discovery jobs.","Use AWS Lake Formation LF-Tags to detect the employee identifier in the data.","Define a custom detection pattern for the EMP- format in the AWS Glue Detect Sensitive Data transform used by the ETL jobs.","Enable Amazon GuardDuty Malware Protection for S3 on the buckets."],"a":[1,3],"e":"Kata kunci: format 'proprietary' (EMP- + 6 digit) yang harus dideteksi di dua tempat: 'objects stored in Amazon S3' dan 'records processed by AWS Glue ETL jobs'. Managed identifier hanya mengenali tipe data umum, sehingga format khusus perusahaan memerlukan pola kustom. Di Macie, custom data identifier berbasis regex (opsional dengan keyword dan jarak) dapat ditambahkan ke discovery job untuk S3. Di Glue, transform Detect Sensitive Data mendukung custom pattern berbasis regex sehingga deteksi terjadi di dalam pipeline sebelum data masuk curated zone. Distraktor terdekat adalah mengandalkan managed data identifiers Macie: tidak ada identifier bawaan untuk format proprietary ini. LF-Tags adalah label untuk kontrol akses, bukan mekanisme deteksi. GuardDuty Malware Protection memindai malware, bukan data sensitif. Aturan umum: pola sensitif khusus perusahaan → custom data identifier (Macie) / custom pattern (Glue).","r":["Salah — Managed data identifiers tidak mengenali format identifier proprietary perusahaan.","Benar — Custom data identifier Macie dengan regex mendeteksi format EMP- di objek S3.","Salah — LF-Tags adalah label untuk otorisasi, bukan alat deteksi isi data.","Benar — Custom pattern di Glue Detect Sensitive Data mendeteksi format tersebut di dalam pipeline ETL.","Salah — GuardDuty Malware Protection memindai malware, bukan PII."],"k":"Tips ujian: format PII khusus → Macie custom data identifier (S3) / Glue custom detection pattern (ETL)."},{"id":"E2C-38","d":2,"ts":"2.4.5","t":"Redshift automatic table optimization","q":"A data engineer is creating a set of new Amazon Redshift tables for a reporting workload whose query patterns are not yet known and are expected to change as new dashboards are added. The engineer wants the tables to perform well without manually re-tuning distribution keys and sort keys over time. Which approach should the engineer use?","o":["Define DISTSTYLE EVEN and no sort key on all tables.","Define an interleaved sort key on every column of each table.","Create the tables with DISTSTYLE AUTO and SORTKEY AUTO so that automatic table optimization adjusts keys based on workload.","Use DISTSTYLE ALL on all tables so that joins never require redistribution."],"a":[2],"e":"Kata kunci soal adalah pola query 'not yet known and are expected to change' serta keinginan untuk tidak 'manually re-tuning distribution keys and sort keys'. Automatic table optimization di Amazon Redshift memantau workload dan secara otomatis menerapkan distribution key dan sort key yang optimal ketika tabel dibuat dengan DISTSTYLE AUTO dan SORTKEY AUTO. Dengan begitu desain fisik menyesuaikan diri tanpa intervensi manual. DISTSTYLE EVEN tanpa sort key tidak memanfaatkan zone maps dan sering memicu redistribusi saat join. Interleaved sort key pada banyak kolom mahal dalam VACUUM REINDEX dan tidak disarankan untuk data yang terus bertambah. DISTSTYLE ALL untuk semua tabel menggandakan tabel besar di setiap node. Aturan umum: pola query tidak diketahui/berubah di Redshift → AUTO untuk distribution style, sort key, dan encoding.","r":["Salah — EVEN tanpa sort key tidak mengoptimalkan join maupun filter.","Salah — Interleaved sort key di banyak kolom mahal dipelihara dan jarang optimal.","Benar — AUTO memungkinkan automatic table optimization menyesuaikan dist key dan sort key berdasarkan workload.","Salah — ALL pada tabel besar memboroskan storage dan memperlambat load."],"k":"Tips ujian: Redshift workload belum diketahui / berubah → DISTSTYLE AUTO + SORTKEY AUTO (automatic table optimization)."},{"id":"E1A-37","d":1,"ts":"1.1.6","t":"S3 Event Notifications vs EventBridge","q":"A data lake bucket receives objects under the raw/ prefix. Three teams need to react to new objects: one team wants all objects under raw/, a second team wants only objects under raw/sales/, and a third team wants only objects larger than 1 GB under raw/. The existing S3 Event Notification configuration fails because of overlapping prefixes. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create three separate buckets and copy each object to the appropriate bucket with a Lambda function.","Enable Amazon EventBridge notifications on the bucket and create three EventBridge rules with event patterns that filter on the object key prefix and object size, each targeting the respective team's consumer.","Configure one S3 Event Notification to an SQS queue and have all three teams poll the same queue.","Enable S3 server access logging and have each team parse the logs."],"a":[1],"e":"Kata kunci: tiga konsumen dengan filter 'overlapping prefixes' dan satu filter berdasarkan 'object size', dengan 'LEAST operational overhead'. S3 Event Notifications tidak mengizinkan konfigurasi dengan prefix yang tumpang tindih untuk tipe event yang sama dan hanya mendukung filter prefix/suffix. Dengan mengaktifkan integrasi Amazon EventBridge pada bucket, semua event objek dikirim ke EventBridge; setiap rule bisa memfilter key prefix, ukuran objek, dan atribut lain, dan satu event dapat cocok dengan banyak rule. Distraktor terdekat adalah satu antrean SQS bersama: setiap pesan hanya diterima oleh satu konsumen, sehingga tim lain kehilangan event. Membuat bucket terpisah dan menyalin objek menambah biaya dan kode. Aturan umum: filtering lanjutan atau banyak target untuk event S3 = S3 → EventBridge.","r":["Salah — Menyalin objek ke banyak bucket menambah biaya penyimpanan, kode, dan latensi.","Benar — EventBridge mendukung pola filter lanjutan (prefix, ukuran) dan banyak rule untuk event yang sama.","Salah — Satu antrean SQS dibagi antar-konsumen, sehingga setiap tim tidak menerima semua event yang relevan.","Salah — Access log dikirim dengan penundaan dan memerlukan parsing kustom."],"k":"Event S3 dengan prefix tumpang tindih / filter ukuran / banyak target → aktifkan S3 → EventBridge."},{"id":"E2A-50","d":2,"ts":"2.1.6","t":"Redshift serializable isolation","q":"Two AWS Glue jobs load data into the same Amazon Redshift tables at overlapping times. Each job runs a multi-statement transaction that reads from and writes to the tables. The jobs intermittently fail with 'ERROR: 1023 Serializable isolation violation on table'. The data engineer wants the jobs to wait for each other instead of failing, without changing the load logic. What should the data engineer do?","o":["Add a LOCK statement for the target tables at the beginning of each job's transaction.","Split each transaction into many autocommit statements.","Run ANALYZE COMPRESSION on the target tables before each load.","Change the tables to DISTSTYLE ALL."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci adalah error 'Serializable isolation violation' dari transaksi konkuren yang membaca dan menulis tabel yang sama, dan keinginan agar job 'wait for each other instead of failing'. Redshift mendeteksi konflik serializable dan membatalkan salah satu transaksi; dokumentasi AWS menyarankan memaksa serialisasi dengan menjalankan perintah LOCK pada tabel yang terlibat di awal transaksi, sehingga transaksi kedua menunggu lock dilepas, bukan gagal. Distraktor terdekat adalah memecah transaksi menjadi autocommit: konflik mungkin berkurang, tetapi atomisitas load hilang dan logika berubah, sehingga kegagalan di tengah jalan meninggalkan data setengah jadi. ANALYZE COMPRESSION dan DISTSTYLE tidak berhubungan dengan isolasi transaksi. Aturan umum: error 1023 di Redshift → serialisasikan dengan LOCK di awal transaksi atau jadwalkan job agar tidak tumpang tindih.","r":["Benar — LOCK di awal transaksi membuat transaksi lain menunggu sehingga konflik serializable tidak terjadi.","Salah — Autocommit per statement menghilangkan atomisitas dan mengubah logika load.","Salah — ANALYZE COMPRESSION hanya menyarankan encoding kolom dan tidak memengaruhi konflik transaksi.","Salah — Gaya distribusi tidak berpengaruh pada isolasi atau konflik transaksi."],"k":"Redshift 'Serializable isolation violation' (1023) → LOCK tables at start of transaction to force serialization."},{"id":"E1B-03","d":1,"ts":"1.2.5","t":"Redshift materialized views for repeated transformations","q":"A company runs an Amazon Redshift provisioned cluster. A sales dashboard runs the same complex query, which joins three large tables and aggregates revenue by region and day, hundreds of times each hour. The base tables receive small batches of inserts throughout the day, and dashboard results should reflect new data within minutes. Analysts work only in SQL. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","o":["Create a Redshift materialized view for the join and aggregation with AUTO REFRESH YES, and point the dashboard at the materialized view.","Run an AWS Glue Spark job every night that computes the aggregates and loads them into a summary table in Redshift.","Create an AWS Lambda function that runs every minute, drops and recreates a summary table with CREATE TABLE AS, and point the dashboard at that table.","UNLOAD the base tables to Amazon S3 every hour and have the dashboard query the files with Amazon Athena."],"a":[0],"e":"Kata kunci penentunya adalah query kompleks yang sama dijalankan 'hundreds of times each hour', data baru harus terlihat 'within minutes', analis 'only in SQL', dan 'LEAST operational overhead'. Materialized view di Redshift menyimpan hasil join dan agregasi yang sudah dihitung sebelumnya, sehingga dashboard membaca hasil siap pakai alih-alih mengulang join besar setiap kali. Dengan opsi AUTO REFRESH YES, Redshift memperbarui materialized view secara otomatis setelah tabel dasar berubah (secara inkremental bila definisinya mendukung), tanpa job atau kode tambahan. Lambda yang membuat ulang tabel setiap menit adalah distraktor terdekat karena hasilnya juga segar, tetapi Anda menulis dan memelihara kode sendiri, dan menghitung ulang seluruh agregasi tiap menit memboroskan sumber daya cluster. Glue job malam hari tidak memenuhi kebutuhan data segar dalam hitungan menit dan menambah layanan di luar SQL. UNLOAD ke S3 lalu Athena memindahkan data keluar dari Redshift dan datanya tertinggal hingga satu jam. Perlu diingat bahwa Redshift memprioritaskan workload pengguna sehingga autorefresh bisa sedikit tertunda; jika butuh jadwal yang deterministik, gunakan REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW terjadwal. Aturan umum: query agregasi berulang di Redshift → materialized view (dengan auto refresh).","r":["Benar — Materialized view menyimpan hasil join/agregasi yang sudah dihitung dan auto refresh menjaganya tetap segar tanpa kode atau pipeline tambahan.","Salah — Glue job malam hari menghasilkan data yang tertinggal hingga sehari dan menambah pipeline di luar SQL.","Salah — Bisa bekerja, tetapi menambah kode kustom dan menghitung ulang seluruh agregasi setiap menit sehingga membebani cluster.","Salah — Memindahkan data keluar dari Redshift, menambah langkah terjadwal, dan data bisa tertinggal hingga satu jam."],"k":"Tips ujian: 'same expensive aggregation query repeated in Redshift, keep results fresh' → materialized view dengan AUTO REFRESH."},{"id":"E2B-17","d":2,"ts":"2.2.4","t":"Non-Hive-style partitions in Athena","q":"A vendor delivers files to Amazon S3 under non-Hive-style prefixes such as s3://vendor-feed/2026/10/14/. A data engineer created an Athena table partitioned by year, month, and day, but MSCK REPAIR TABLE does not add any partitions. Which TWO solutions will make the data queryable by partition in Amazon Athena? (Choose TWO.)","o":["Run ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION statements that map each partition value to its S3 LOCATION.","Configure partition projection on the table with a storage.location.template that matches the vendor's prefix format.","Run MSCK REPAIR TABLE with a larger query timeout.","Enable S3 Versioning on the bucket so that Athena can detect new prefixes.","Recreate the table without partition keys and add a WHERE clause on the S3 object key."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Kata kunci: 'non-Hive-style prefixes' dan 'MSCK REPAIR TABLE does not add any partitions'. MSCK REPAIR hanya mengenali path berbentuk key=value, jadi path 2026/10/14 tidak terdeteksi berapa pun timeout-nya. ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION ... LOCATION memetakan setiap nilai partisi ke folder tertentu secara eksplisit, sehingga bekerja untuk path apa pun. Partition projection dengan storage.location.template (misalnya s3://vendor-feed/${year}/${month}/${day}/) membuat Athena menghitung lokasi partisi dari konfigurasi tanpa perlu mendaftarkannya. Versioning S3 tidak berhubungan dengan metadata partisi. Tabel tanpa partisi kehilangan partition pruning, sehingga biaya scan naik. Ingat: non-Hive-style path → ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION dengan LOCATION, atau partition projection dengan location template.","r":["Benar — ADD PARTITION dengan LOCATION eksplisit bekerja untuk struktur folder apa pun.","Benar — Partition projection dengan storage.location.template memetakan nilai partisi ke path non-Hive-style.","Salah — MSCK REPAIR hanya mengenali path key=value; timeout lebih lama tidak mengubah itu.","Salah — Versioning tidak berhubungan dengan deteksi atau pendaftaran partisi.","Salah — Tanpa partisi, Athena memindai seluruh data dan biaya query naik."],"k":"Tips ujian: path tanpa 'key=value' → MSCK tidak bisa; pakai ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION ... LOCATION atau partition projection."}]});